window.I3_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"Climate Science & the Atmosphere 氣候科學與大氣","cards":[{"w":"climate","p":"n.","d":"the usual weather of a place over many years","c":"氣候","s":"Taiwan has a warm and wet climate, so many visitors from Europe find the summer months hard to handle at first.","t":"台灣擁有溫暖潮濕的氣候,所以許多來自歐洲的遊客一開始會覺得夏季幾個月很難適應。"},{"w":"atmosphere","p":"n.","d":"the layer of gases around the Earth","c":"大氣層","s":"Scientists explained that the atmosphere works like a warm blanket around the Earth, but too much carbon makes the blanket thicker.","t":"科學家解釋說,大氣層就像包覆地球的一條溫暖毯子,但太多的碳會讓這條毯子變得更厚。"},{"w":"atmospheric","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the air around the Earth","c":"大氣的","s":"The research team measures atmospheric pressure every hour, because sudden changes often tell them that a storm is coming.","t":"研究團隊每小時測量一次大氣壓力,因為突然的變化常常告訴他們暴風雨即將來臨。"},{"w":"temperature","p":"n.","d":"how hot or cold something is","c":"溫度;氣溫","s":"The average temperature in Taipei has risen over the past fifty years, and many older residents say summers feel much longer now.","t":"台北的平均氣溫在過去五十年間上升了,許多年長居民說現在的夏天感覺長了許多。"},{"w":"humidity","p":"n.","d":"the amount of water in the air","c":"濕度","s":"The humidity was over ninety percent this afternoon, so my clothes would not dry and the whole apartment felt sticky.","t":"今天下午的濕度超過百分之九十,所以我的衣服乾不了,整間公寓都感覺黏黏的。"},{"w":"humid","p":"adj.","d":"hot and wet in an uncomfortable way","c":"潮濕悶熱的","s":"July in southern Taiwan is extremely hot and humid, so we always carry a towel and plenty of water when we go out.","t":"南台灣的七月非常炎熱又潮濕悶熱,所以我們出門時總是帶著毛巾和充足的水。"},{"w":"precipitation","p":"n.","d":"rain, snow or hail that falls from the sky","c":"降水(量)","s":"Climate models show that precipitation will become less regular, so some months may be very dry while others bring heavy rain.","t":"氣候模型顯示降水將變得較不規律,因此有些月份可能非常乾燥,而另一些月份則會帶來大雨。"},{"w":"rainfall","p":"n.","d":"the amount of rain that falls in a place","c":"降雨量","s":"Farmers in the area depend on spring rainfall for their rice fields, but last year the rain arrived almost a month late.","t":"這地區的農夫依賴春季降雨量來灌溉稻田,但去年雨水幾乎晚了一個月才來。"},{"w":"evaporate","p":"v.","d":"to change from liquid into gas","c":"蒸發","s":"During the heatwave, the water in the small pond began to evaporate quickly, and the frogs had to look for a new home.","t":"熱浪期間,小池塘裡的水開始迅速蒸發,青蛙們只好去找新的家。"},{"w":"evaporation","p":"n.","d":"the process of water turning into gas","c":"蒸發(作用)","s":"Higher temperatures increase evaporation from lakes and soil, so reservoirs can lose water even when nobody is using it.","t":"較高的氣溫會增加湖泊和土壤的蒸發,因此即使沒有人使用,水庫也可能流失水量。"},{"w":"condensation","p":"n.","d":"water drops that form when warm air touches something cold","c":"凝結(水珠)","s":"There was a lot of condensation on the bathroom window this morning, because the hot shower filled the cold room with steam.","t":"今天早上浴室窗戶上有很多凝結的水珠,因為熱水澡讓冰冷的房間充滿了蒸氣。"},{"w":"moisture","p":"n.","d":"a small amount of water in the air or in something","c":"濕氣;水分","s":"Warm air can hold more moisture than cold air, which is one reason why storms are becoming heavier in a warmer world.","t":"暖空氣能比冷空氣容納更多水氣,這就是在更暖的世界裡暴風雨變得更猛烈的原因之一。"},{"w":"ozone","p":"n.","d":"a gas high in the sky that blocks harmful sunlight","c":"臭氧","s":"The layer of ozone high above us protects our skin from strong sunlight, and countries worked together to repair the hole in it.","t":"我們頭頂高空中的臭氧層保護我們的皮膚免受強烈陽光傷害,各國也曾合作修補它的破洞。"},{"w":"ultraviolet","p":"adj.","d":"describing invisible light from the sun that can burn skin","c":"紫外線的","s":"The weather app warned that ultraviolet levels would be very high at noon, so the coach moved our practice to the evening.","t":"天氣應用程式警告中午的紫外線指數會非常高,所以教練把我們的練習改到傍晚。"},{"w":"radiation","p":"n.","d":"energy that travels as heat or light","c":"輻射","s":"The Earth receives radiation from the sun every day, and some of this energy should escape back into space at night.","t":"地球每天接收來自太陽的輻射,而其中一部分能量應該在夜間散逸回太空。"},{"w":"solar","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the sun","c":"太陽的","s":"Our school installed solar lights along the path to the gym, and they charge during the day and shine all night.","t":"我們學校在通往體育館的小路旁裝了太陽能燈,它們白天充電,整晚都會發光。"},{"w":"meteorologist","p":"n.","d":"a scientist who studies and reports the weather","c":"氣象學家;氣象預報員","s":"The TV meteorologist said the typhoon would turn north, but many people still bought extra food and water just in case.","t":"電視上的氣象預報員說颱風會轉向北方,但許多人還是買了額外的食物和水以防萬一。"},{"w":"climatologist","p":"n.","d":"a scientist who studies climate over long periods","c":"氣候學家","s":"A climatologist visited our class and showed us old temperature records, so we could see how much the island has warmed.","t":"一位氣候學家來到我們班上,給我們看舊的氣溫紀錄,讓我們看見這座島已經變暖了多少。"},{"w":"thermometer","p":"n.","d":"a tool that measures temperature","c":"溫度計","s":"The thermometer outside our classroom showed thirty-six degrees, so the principal let everyone stay inside during the break.","t":"我們教室外的溫度計顯示三十六度,所以校長讓大家下課時都待在室內。"},{"w":"Celsius","p":"n.","d":"a scale for measuring temperature where water freezes at 0","c":"攝氏","s":"World leaders hope to keep warming below 1.5 degrees Celsius, but many experts believe this goal is becoming very difficult.","t":"世界領袖希望把暖化控制在攝氏1.5度以下,但許多專家認為這個目標正變得非常困難。"},{"w":"anomaly","p":"n.","d":"something that is different from what is normal","c":"異常(現象)","s":"A warm winter used to be an anomaly in this region, but now it happens almost every year and nobody is surprised.","t":"暖冬過去在這個地區是一種異常現象,但現在幾乎每年都會發生,也沒有人感到驚訝了。"},{"w":"seasonal","p":"adj.","d":"happening at a particular time of the year","c":"季節性的","s":"Many farmers hire seasonal workers in the summer, but the harvest now starts earlier because the spring is warmer.","t":"許多農夫在夏天雇用季節性工人,但因為春天變得較暖,收成現在提早開始了。"},{"w":"monsoon","p":"n.","d":"the season of heavy rain in South and Southeast Asia","c":"季風(雨季)","s":"The monsoon brings most of the year's rain to India, so a weak season can hurt millions of farmers and their families.","t":"季風為印度帶來一年中大部分的雨量,所以雨季偏弱時可能會傷害數百萬農民和他們的家庭。"},{"w":"tropical","p":"adj.","d":"from the hot area near the equator","c":"熱帶的","s":"tropical diseases such as dengue fever are spreading north, because mosquitoes can now survive in places that were once too cool.","t":"像登革熱這樣的熱帶疾病正向北擴散,因為蚊子現在能在曾經太涼爽的地方存活。"},{"w":"arid","p":"adj.","d":"very dry with little rain","c":"乾旱的;乾燥的","s":"The farm is in an arid part of the country, so the family collects every drop of rain and grows plants that need little water.","t":"這座農場位於國內乾旱的地區,所以這家人收集每一滴雨水,並種植需水量少的植物。"},{"w":"temperate","p":"adj.","d":"not very hot and not very cold","c":"溫和的;溫帶的","s":"Britain has a temperate climate, but recent summers have been so hot that train tracks bent and some roads began to melt.","t":"英國屬於溫帶氣候,但最近幾個夏天熱到鐵軌彎曲,有些道路也開始融化。"},{"w":"polar","p":"adj.","d":"near the North or South Pole","c":"極地的","s":"polar regions are warming faster than the rest of the planet, and this change affects weather patterns far away.","t":"極地地區暖化的速度比地球其他地方更快,而這種變化會影響遠方的天氣型態。"},{"w":"latitude","p":"n.","d":"the distance of a place north or south of the equator","c":"緯度","s":"Some plants are moving to higher latitude as the climate warms, but slow-growing trees often cannot move fast enough.","t":"隨著氣候變暖,有些植物正往較高緯度遷移,但生長緩慢的樹木往往移動得不夠快。"},{"w":"altitude","p":"n.","d":"the height of a place above sea level","c":"海拔;高度","s":"Tea farmers in Taiwan are planting at higher altitude now, because the lower hills have become too warm for good leaves.","t":"台灣的茶農現在都種在更高的海拔,因為較低的山丘已經變得太熱,長不出好的茶葉。"},{"w":"jet stream","p":"n.phr.","d":"a strong, fast wind high in the sky","c":"噴射氣流","s":"When the jet stream gets weak and wavy, hot or cold weather can stay in one place for many days.","t":"當噴射氣流變弱並呈波浪狀時,炎熱或寒冷的天氣可能會在同一個地方停留許多天。"}]},{"unit":2,"theme":"Greenhouse Gases & Emissions 溫室氣體與排放","cards":[{"w":"greenhouse gas","p":"n.phr.","d":"a gas that traps heat in the atmosphere","c":"溫室氣體","s":"Carbon dioxide is the most common greenhouse gas, but methane from farms is also a serious problem.","t":"二氧化碳是最常見的溫室氣體,但來自農場的甲烷也是一個嚴重的問題。"},{"w":"emission","p":"n.","d":"gas or smoke that is sent into the air","c":"排放(物)","s":"The city wants to cut its emission by half before 2035, so it is adding more bus lanes and bike paths.","t":"這座城市想在2035年前把排放量減半,所以正在增加更多公車專用道和自行車道。"},{"w":"emit","p":"v.","d":"to send out gas, heat, light or sound","c":"排放;散發","s":"Old motorcycles emit much more smoke than new electric scooters, so the government gives money to people who replace them.","t":"舊機車排放的廢氣比新的電動機車多得多,所以政府會補助汰換的民眾。"},{"w":"carbon","p":"n.","d":"a chemical element found in coal, oil and living things","c":"碳","s":"Trees store carbon in their wood and leaves, so cutting down forests releases it back into the air.","t":"樹木把碳儲存在木材和葉子裡,所以砍伐森林會把它釋放回空氣中。"},{"w":"carbon dioxide","p":"n.phr.","d":"the gas CO2, produced when fuel is burned","c":"二氧化碳","s":"Every time we drive a petrol car, it releases carbon dioxide, and this gas stays in the air for hundreds of years.","t":"每次我們開汽油車,它都會釋放二氧化碳,而這種氣體會在空氣中停留數百年。"},{"w":"methane","p":"n.","d":"a strong greenhouse gas from farms, rubbish and gas fields","c":"甲烷","s":"Cows produce a lot of methane when they digest grass, so some farmers are testing new kinds of animal food.","t":"牛在消化草時會產生大量甲烷,所以有些農夫正在測試新型的動物飼料。"},{"w":"fossil fuel","p":"n.phr.","d":"coal, oil or gas formed from ancient plants and animals","c":"化石燃料","s":"Most power plants still burn fossil fuel, but the share of clean energy is growing every year.","t":"大多數發電廠仍在燃燒化石燃料,但潔淨能源的比例每年都在成長。"},{"w":"coal","p":"n.","d":"a hard black rock burned to make heat or electricity","c":"煤","s":"The old power station burned coal for forty years, but it will close next year and become a museum.","t":"這座老舊發電廠燒煤燒了四十年,但它明年將關閉並改建為博物館。"},{"w":"petroleum","p":"n.","d":"oil from under the ground used to make fuel and plastic","c":"石油","s":"Many everyday products are made from petroleum, so reducing plastic also helps to reduce our use of oil.","t":"許多日常用品都是由石油製成的,所以減少塑膠也有助於減少我們對石油的使用。"},{"w":"exhaust","p":"n.","d":"waste gas that comes out of an engine","c":"(引擎)廢氣","s":"The exhaust from the buses made the air near the station dirty, so the city switched to electric buses last year.","t":"公車排出的廢氣讓車站附近的空氣很髒,所以市政府去年改用電動公車。"},{"w":"fumes","p":"n.","d":"strong, unpleasant smoke or gas","c":"(有害的)煙霧;廢氣","s":"The fumes from the factory smelled terrible, so local parents asked the company to clean its chimneys.","t":"工廠排出的煙霧聞起來很可怕,所以當地家長要求公司清理煙囪。"},{"w":"smog","p":"n.","d":"dirty air that looks like fog over a city","c":"霧霾;煙霧","s":"Thick smog covered the city for three days, so schools cancelled outdoor sports and many people wore masks.","t":"濃厚的霧霾籠罩城市三天,所以學校取消了戶外運動,許多人也戴上口罩。"},{"w":"soot","p":"n.","d":"black powder made when something is burned","c":"煤灰;煙灰","s":"Black soot from wildfires lands on snow and ice, and the dark surface then melts faster in the sun.","t":"野火產生的黑色煙灰落在雪和冰上,而深色的表面在陽光下就會融化得更快。"},{"w":"combustion","p":"n.","d":"the process of burning","c":"燃燒","s":"Cars with combustion engines burn fuel to move, but electric cars use batteries and produce no smoke on the road.","t":"使用燃燒式引擎的汽車靠燃燒燃料來行駛,但電動車使用電池,在路上不會產生廢氣。"},{"w":"absorb","p":"v.","d":"to take in something such as liquid, heat or gas","c":"吸收","s":"The ocean can absorb a lot of heat, but warmer water then causes problems for fish and other sea life.","t":"海洋能吸收大量的熱,但較暖的海水接著會為魚類和其他海洋生物帶來問題。"},{"w":"absorption","p":"n.","d":"the process of taking something in","c":"吸收(作用)","s":"Dark roofs increase the absorption of heat, so painting them white can keep a building several degrees cooler.","t":"深色屋頂會增加熱的吸收,所以把它們漆成白色可以讓建築物涼爽好幾度。"},{"w":"heat-trapping","p":"adj.","d":"keeping heat in and not letting it escape","c":"吸熱的;困住熱能的","s":"These heat-trapping gases act like the glass of a car in summer, and the temperature inside keeps rising.","t":"這些困住熱能的氣體就像夏天汽車的玻璃,而裡面的溫度會不斷上升。"},{"w":"smokestack","p":"n.","d":"a tall chimney on a factory","c":"(工廠)煙囪","s":"Grey smoke rose from the tall smokestack all night, and the neighbours complained that their washing turned dirty.","t":"灰色煙霧整夜從高高的煙囪冒出,鄰居抱怨他們晾的衣服都變髒了。"},{"w":"tailpipe","p":"n.","d":"the pipe at the back of a car where exhaust comes out","c":"(汽車)排氣管","s":"Electric cars have no tailpipe, but the electricity they use may still come from coal power stations.","t":"電動車沒有排氣管,但它們使用的電力可能仍來自燃煤發電廠。"},{"w":"landfill","p":"n.","d":"a place where rubbish is buried in the ground","c":"垃圾掩埋場","s":"Food waste in a landfill produces methane as it rots, so our town now collects kitchen scraps separately.","t":"垃圾掩埋場裡的廚餘在腐爛時會產生甲烷,所以我們鎮上現在把廚餘分開收集。"},{"w":"fertiliser","p":"n.","d":"a substance added to soil to help plants grow","c":"肥料","s":"Too much fertiliser washes into rivers when it rains, and it also releases a gas that warms the planet.","t":"下雨時過多的肥料會被沖進河川,而且它也會釋放一種使地球變暖的氣體。"},{"w":"refinery","p":"n.","d":"a factory where oil is made into fuel","c":"煉油廠","s":"The new refinery will create many jobs, but environmental groups worry about the extra pollution it will bring.","t":"新的煉油廠將創造許多工作機會,但環保團體擔心它會帶來額外的污染。"},{"w":"pollute","p":"v.","d":"to make air, water or land dirty","c":"污染","s":"Factories that pollute the river must now pay large fines, so many of them have started to clean their waste water.","t":"污染河川的工廠現在必須繳納高額罰款,所以其中許多已開始處理它們的廢水。"},{"w":"carbon sink","p":"n.phr.","d":"a forest, ocean or soil that takes in more carbon than it gives out","c":"碳匯","s":"The mangrove forest is an important carbon sink, so the village protects it and plants new trees every spring.","t":"紅樹林是一個重要的碳匯,所以村民保護它,並在每年春天種植新樹。"},{"w":"decarbonise","p":"v.","d":"to reduce the carbon a country or company produces","c":"去碳化;減碳","s":"The steel company promised to decarbonise its factories by 2050, but critics say the plan has no clear steps.","t":"這家鋼鐵公司承諾在2050年前讓工廠去碳化,但批評者說這個計畫沒有明確的步驟。"},{"w":"aerosol","p":"n.","d":"tiny drops or bits floating in the air","c":"氣溶膠;懸浮微粒","s":"Some aerosol from volcanoes can cool the planet for a short time, but they do not solve the problem of global warming.","t":"某些來自火山的懸浮微粒能讓地球短暫降溫,但它們無法解決全球暖化的問題。"},{"w":"incinerate","p":"v.","d":"to burn something completely, especially rubbish","c":"焚化","s":"Many cities incinerate their rubbish to save space, but burning plastic releases carbon and other harmful gases.","t":"許多城市焚化垃圾以節省空間,但燃燒塑膠會釋放碳和其他有害氣體。"},{"w":"industrialised","p":"adj.","d":"having many factories and industries","c":"工業化的","s":"industrialised countries have produced most of the carbon in the past, so poorer nations say the rich should pay more for solutions.","t":"工業化國家過去製造了大部分的碳,所以較貧窮的國家說富國應該為解決方案付出更多。"}]},{"unit":3,"theme":"Extreme Weather & Natural Hazards 極端天氣與自然災害","cards":[{"w":"sweltering","p":"adj.","d":"extremely hot and uncomfortable","c":"酷熱難耐的","s":"It was a sweltering afternoon at the bus stop, and an old man nearly fainted before the bus finally arrived.","t":"公車站那天下午酷熱難耐,一位老先生在公車終於到站前差點昏倒。"},{"w":"heatwave","p":"n.","d":"a period of unusually hot weather","c":"熱浪","s":"During the heatwave last August, hospitals were full of elderly patients, so the city opened cool rooms in libraries.","t":"去年八月的熱浪期間,醫院擠滿了年長的病人,所以市政府在圖書館開設了降溫室。"},{"w":"typhoon","p":"n.","d":"a violent tropical storm in the western Pacific","c":"颱風","s":"Schools were closed because a strong typhoon was approaching, but my little brother was disappointed that it only rained a little.","t":"因為一個強烈颱風正在接近,學校停課了,但我弟弟很失望因為只下了一點雨。"},{"w":"hurricane","p":"n.","d":"a violent tropical storm in the Atlantic","c":"颶風","s":"The hurricane destroyed hundreds of homes in Florida, and many families had to live in hotels for months.","t":"颶風摧毀了佛羅里達州數百棟房屋,許多家庭不得不在旅館住上好幾個月。"},{"w":"cyclone","p":"n.","d":"a violent storm with strong circular winds","c":"氣旋;熱帶風暴","s":"A powerful cyclone hit the coast of Bangladesh, but early warnings helped thousands of people reach safety in time.","t":"一個強大的氣旋襲擊了孟加拉沿岸,但及早的警報幫助數千人及時抵達安全處。"},{"w":"tornado","p":"n.","d":"a narrow, spinning column of wind that destroys things","c":"龍捲風","s":"The tornado lifted cars into the air, yet the family survived because they hid in the basement.","t":"龍捲風把汽車捲到空中,但這家人因為躲在地下室而倖存。"},{"w":"storm surge","p":"n.phr.","d":"a sudden rise of sea water pushed by a storm","c":"風暴潮","s":"The storm surge pushed seawater two metres into the streets, so many ground-floor shops were completely ruined.","t":"風暴潮把海水推進街道達兩公尺高,所以許多一樓的店家完全被毀。"},{"w":"flood","p":"v.","d":"to cover an area with water","c":"淹沒;淹水","s":"Heavy rain flood the underground car park, and dozens of cars were stuck under the water until the next day.","t":"大雨淹沒了地下停車場,數十輛汽車被困在水下直到隔天。"},{"w":"downpour","p":"n.","d":"a sudden heavy fall of rain","c":"傾盆大雨","s":"We were caught in a sudden downpour on the way home, and our school bags were completely soaked.","t":"我們在回家的路上遇到一場突如其來的傾盆大雨,書包全都濕透了。"},{"w":"torrential","p":"adj.","d":"used to describe very heavy rain","c":"(雨)傾盆的;猛烈的","s":"torrential rain fell for twelve hours, so the river rose quickly and the bridge had to be closed.","t":"傾盆大雨下了十二個小時,所以河水迅速上漲,橋也不得不封閉。"},{"w":"landslide","p":"n.","d":"a mass of earth and rocks falling down a hill","c":"山崩;土石流","s":"A landslide blocked the mountain road after the typhoon, and the villagers had no fresh food for a week.","t":"颱風過後一場山崩堵住了山路,村民們一週都沒有新鮮的食物。"},{"w":"mudslide","p":"n.","d":"a flow of wet mud down a hill","c":"泥流;土石流","s":"The hillside had lost its trees, so the heavy rain caused a mudslide that buried several houses.","t":"山坡的樹木已經沒了,所以大雨引發了一場土石流,掩埋了好幾棟房子。"},{"w":"avalanche","p":"n.","d":"a large amount of snow falling down a mountain","c":"雪崩","s":"Warmer winters make the snow less stable, so the risk of an avalanche is higher for skiers in spring.","t":"較暖的冬天讓積雪較不穩定,所以春季滑雪者遇到雪崩的風險更高。"},{"w":"blizzard","p":"n.","d":"a severe snowstorm with strong wind","c":"暴風雪","s":"The blizzard closed the airport for two days, and thousands of travellers slept on the floor of the terminal.","t":"暴風雪讓機場關閉了兩天,數千名旅客睡在航廈的地板上。"},{"w":"hailstorm","p":"n.","d":"a storm in which balls of ice fall from the sky","c":"冰雹暴","s":"A sudden hailstorm damaged the fruit on the trees, so the farmer lost almost half of his apples.","t":"一場突如其來的冰雹打壞了樹上的果實,所以這位農夫損失了將近一半的蘋果。"},{"w":"lightning","p":"n.","d":"a bright flash of electricity in the sky during a storm","c":"閃電","s":"lightning struck a tree near the playground, so the teacher told all the students to go inside at once.","t":"閃電擊中了遊樂場附近的一棵樹,所以老師叫所有學生立刻進到室內。"},{"w":"thunderstorm","p":"n.","d":"a storm with thunder, lightning and heavy rain","c":"雷雨","s":"Afternoon thunderstorm are common in Taipei in summer, so I always keep an umbrella in my backpack.","t":"夏天的台北常有午後雷雨,所以我總是在背包裡放一把傘。"},{"w":"gust","p":"n.","d":"a sudden strong rush of wind","c":"一陣強風","s":"A strong gust of wind turned my umbrella inside out, and everyone at the bus stop started laughing.","t":"一陣強風把我的傘吹得翻了過來,公車站的每個人都笑了起來。"},{"w":"evacuate","p":"v.","d":"to move people away from a dangerous place","c":"撤離;疏散","s":"Officials decided to evacuate the coastal village before the storm arrived, but some old fishermen refused to leave.","t":"官員決定在暴風雨來臨前撤離沿海村莊,但有些老漁夫拒絕離開。"},{"w":"evacuation","p":"n.","d":"the act of moving people to a safe place","c":"撤離;疏散","s":"The school practises an evacuation plan twice a year, so every student knows which exit to use in an emergency.","t":"學校每年演練兩次疏散計畫,所以每位學生都知道緊急時要走哪個出口。"},{"w":"shelter","p":"n.","d":"a place that protects people from danger or bad weather","c":"避難所","s":"The town turned the sports centre into a shelter, and volunteers gave out blankets and hot meals all night.","t":"鎮上把運動中心改成避難所,志工們整晚發放毛毯和熱食。"},{"w":"casualty","p":"n.","d":"a person who is hurt or killed in an accident or disaster","c":"傷亡者","s":"The storm was very strong, but there were few casualty because people had left the area in time.","t":"暴風雨非常強烈,但由於人們及時離開了該地區,傷亡人數很少。"},{"w":"disaster","p":"n.","d":"a sudden event that causes great damage","c":"災難","s":"The flood was the worst disaster in the town's history, and it took three years to rebuild the main street.","t":"這場洪水是鎮上有史以來最嚴重的災難,重建主要街道花了三年時間。"},{"w":"catastrophic","p":"adj.","d":"causing terrible damage","c":"災難性的","s":"Scientists warn that warming of three degrees could have catastrophic effects, so they want governments to act now.","t":"科學家警告升溫三度可能帶來災難性的影響,所以他們希望各國政府現在就採取行動。"},{"w":"devastate","p":"v.","d":"to destroy or damage something very badly","c":"摧毀;使荒廢","s":"The wildfire devastate the small mountain town, but the residents promised to rebuild it together.","t":"野火摧毀了這座山中小鎮,但居民們承諾要一起重建它。"},{"w":"hazard","p":"n.","d":"something that may be dangerous","c":"危險;危害","s":"Fallen power lines are a serious hazard after a typhoon, so children should never touch anything on the ground.","t":"颱風過後倒下的電線是嚴重的危險,所以孩子們絕不應該碰觸地上的任何東西。"},{"w":"frequency","p":"n.","d":"how often something happens","c":"頻率","s":"The frequency of strong typhoons has increased in recent years, and insurance companies have raised their prices.","t":"近年來強烈颱風的頻率增加了,保險公司也提高了保費。"},{"w":"severity","p":"n.","d":"how serious or bad something is","c":"嚴重程度","s":"Nobody expected the severity of the flooding, so many families did not move their cars or furniture in time.","t":"沒有人預料到淹水的嚴重程度,所以許多家庭沒有及時移走他們的車子或家具。"},{"w":"heatstroke","p":"n.","d":"a dangerous illness caused by too much heat","c":"中暑","s":"Two runners suffered from heatstroke during the summer race, so the organisers moved the next event to early morning.","t":"兩名跑者在夏季賽跑中中暑,所以主辦單位把下一場比賽改到清晨。"},{"w":"dry spell","p":"n.phr.","d":"a period with no rain","c":"乾旱期;久旱","s":"After a long dry spell, the farmers were happy to see rain, but the hard ground could not absorb it.","t":"經過長時間的乾旱期,農夫們很高興看到下雨,但乾硬的土地無法吸收雨水。"}]},{"unit":4,"theme":"Oceans, Ice & Rising Seas 海洋、冰層與海平面上升","cards":[{"w":"glacier","p":"n.","d":"a large mass of ice that moves slowly down a mountain","c":"冰河","s":"My grandparents visited the glacier forty years ago, and when we went there last summer it was much smaller.","t":"我的祖父母四十年前造訪過那座冰河,而我們去年夏天去的時候它已經小了很多。"},{"w":"ice sheet","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very large, thick layer of ice covering land","c":"冰原;冰蓋","s":"The ice sheet in Greenland is losing billions of tonnes of ice each year, and this water raises the sea.","t":"格陵蘭的冰原每年流失數十億噸的冰,而這些水會使海平面上升。"},{"w":"iceberg","p":"n.","d":"a huge piece of ice floating in the sea","c":"冰山","s":"A giant iceberg broke away from Antarctica last year, and it was bigger than the city of Taipei.","t":"去年一座巨大的冰山從南極洲斷裂分離,它比台北市還要大。"},{"w":"permafrost","p":"n.","d":"ground that stays frozen all year","c":"永凍土","s":"As the permafrost melts, roads and houses in northern Russia are sinking, and old gases escape into the air.","t":"隨著永凍土融化,俄羅斯北部的道路和房屋正在下陷,古老的氣體也逸散到空氣中。"},{"w":"thaw","p":"v.","d":"to change from ice to water; to stop being frozen","c":"解凍;融化","s":"The lake used to stay frozen until April, but now it starts to thaw in early March.","t":"這座湖過去會一直結冰到四月,但現在三月初就開始解凍了。"},{"w":"melt","p":"v.","d":"to change from solid to liquid because of heat","c":"融化","s":"The snow on the mountain melt earlier every year, so the river has less water in the dry summer months.","t":"山上的雪每年都更早融化,所以河川在乾燥的夏季月份水量變少了。"},{"w":"meltwater","p":"n.","d":"water from melting snow or ice","c":"融水;雪水","s":"Villages in the Himalayas depend on meltwater from glaciers, but this supply may disappear within a few decades.","t":"喜馬拉雅山區的村莊依賴冰河的融水,但這項水源可能在幾十年內消失。"},{"w":"sea level","p":"n.phr.","d":"the average height of the sea's surface","c":"海平面","s":"The sea level around this island has risen by about twenty centimetres, and high tides now reach the main road.","t":"這座島周圍的海平面上升了約二十公分,現在漲潮時海水已經到達主要道路。"},{"w":"coastline","p":"n.","d":"the land along the edge of the sea","c":"海岸線","s":"Taiwan has a long and beautiful coastline, but some beaches are disappearing because the sea is rising.","t":"台灣擁有漫長而美麗的海岸線,但有些海灘正因海平面上升而消失。"},{"w":"coastal","p":"adj.","d":"on or near the sea coast","c":"沿海的","s":"Many coastal cities are building higher walls, because storms push seawater further inland than before.","t":"許多沿海城市正在建造更高的牆,因為暴風雨把海水推得比以前更深入內陸。"},{"w":"low-lying","p":"adj.","d":"close to sea level","c":"地勢低窪的","s":"The family sold their house in a low-lying area, because the street flooded every time there was a heavy storm.","t":"這家人賣掉了他們位在地勢低窪地區的房子,因為每次大暴雨街道都會淹水。"},{"w":"submerge","p":"v.","d":"to go or put completely under water","c":"淹沒;沉入水中","s":"Some Pacific islands may be submerge by the end of the century, so their governments are already planning for the future.","t":"一些太平洋島嶼可能在本世紀末被淹沒,所以它們的政府已經在為未來做規劃。"},{"w":"inundate","p":"v.","d":"to flood an area with water","c":"淹沒;泛濫","s":"Seawater inundate the rice fields during the storm, and the salt made the soil useless for several years.","t":"暴風雨期間海水淹沒了稻田,而鹽分讓土壤好幾年都無法使用。"},{"w":"tide","p":"n.","d":"the regular rise and fall of the sea","c":"潮汐;潮水","s":"When the tide is high and it rains heavily, the drains cannot empty, so the streets of the old town flood.","t":"當潮水很高又下大雨時,排水溝無法排空,所以老城區的街道就會淹水。"},{"w":"tidal","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the rise and fall of the sea","c":"潮汐的","s":"The tidal flat near our town is full of crabs and birds, but rising water may cover it completely one day.","t":"我們鎮附近的潮間灘地充滿了螃蟹和鳥類,但上升的海水有一天可能會把它完全淹沒。"},{"w":"acidification","p":"n.","d":"the process of becoming more acidic","c":"酸化","s":"Ocean acidification makes it harder for shellfish to build their shells, so oyster farmers are very worried.","t":"海洋酸化讓貝類更難形成外殼,所以牡蠣養殖戶非常擔心。"},{"w":"acidic","p":"adj.","d":"containing acid; sour","c":"酸性的","s":"The sea is becoming more acidic because it absorbs carbon dioxide, and this change harms tiny sea creatures.","t":"海洋因為吸收二氧化碳而變得更酸,這種變化傷害了微小的海洋生物。"},{"w":"bleaching","p":"n.","d":"the loss of colour in coral when the water is too warm","c":"(珊瑚)白化","s":"Divers in Kenting saw serious coral bleaching last summer, because the sea temperature stayed high for weeks.","t":"去年夏天潛水員在墾丁看到嚴重的珊瑚白化,因為海水溫度連續好幾週居高不下。"},{"w":"current","p":"n.","d":"a steady flow of water in one direction","c":"洋流;水流","s":"Ocean current carry warm water around the world, and if they slow down, the weather in Europe could change.","t":"洋流把溫暖的海水帶到世界各地,如果它們減緩,歐洲的天氣可能會改變。"},{"w":"Arctic","p":"n.","d":"the area around the North Pole","c":"北極地區","s":"The Arctic is warming almost four times faster than the rest of the world, so polar bears are losing their hunting grounds.","t":"北極地區暖化的速度幾乎是世界其他地方的四倍,所以北極熊正在失去牠們的獵食場。"},{"w":"Antarctic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the area around the South Pole","c":"南極的","s":"Scientists live at Antarctic research stations for months, and they study the ice to learn about past climates.","t":"科學家在南極研究站住上好幾個月,他們研究冰層以了解過去的氣候。"},{"w":"ice cap","p":"n.phr.","d":"a thick layer of ice covering a large area","c":"冰帽;冰冠","s":"The polar ice cap reflect sunlight back into space, but as they shrink, the dark sea absorbs more heat.","t":"極地冰帽會把陽光反射回太空,但當它們縮小時,深色的海洋就會吸收更多熱。"},{"w":"salinity","p":"n.","d":"the amount of salt in water","c":"鹽度","s":"Melting ice lowers the salinity of the ocean, and this can change the way water moves around the planet.","t":"融化的冰會降低海洋的鹽度,而這可能改變海水在地球上流動的方式。"},{"w":"sea ice","p":"n.phr.","d":"frozen sea water floating on the ocean","c":"海冰","s":"Polar bears hunt seals on the sea ice, but it now melts earlier in spring and forms later in autumn.","t":"北極熊在海冰上獵捕海豹,但現在海冰春天融化得更早,秋天也更晚形成。"},{"w":"thermal expansion","p":"n.phr.","d":"the way water takes up more space when it gets warmer","c":"熱膨脹","s":"Part of sea level rise comes from thermal expansion, because warm water takes up more space than cold water.","t":"海平面上升有一部分來自熱膨脹,因為溫暖的水比冷水占據更多空間。"},{"w":"delta","p":"n.","d":"flat land where a river divides before entering the sea","c":"三角洲","s":"Millions of people farm in the Mekong delta, but salty seawater is now reaching their rice fields.","t":"數百萬人在湄公河三角洲務農,但鹹的海水現在已經流進他們的稻田。"}]},{"unit":5,"theme":"Impacts on People & Nature 對人類與自然的影響","cards":[{"w":"famine","p":"n.","d":"a serious lack of food in a large area","c":"饑荒","s":"Years without rain led to famine in parts of East Africa, so aid groups sent food and clean water.","t":"多年不下雨導致東非部分地區發生饑荒,所以援助團體送去了食物和乾淨的水。"},{"w":"scarcity","p":"n.","d":"a situation in which there is not enough of something","c":"缺乏;短缺","s":"Water scarcity is a growing problem in many cities, and some families can only use tap water on certain days.","t":"水資源短缺在許多城市是一個日益嚴重的問題,有些家庭只能在特定日子使用自來水。"},{"w":"water stress","p":"n.phr.","d":"when people need more water than is available","c":"缺水壓力;水資源壓力","s":"Regions under high water stress must save every drop, so farmers there are switching to crops that need less water.","t":"處於高度缺水壓力的地區必須節約每一滴水,所以那裡的農夫正改種需水量較少的作物。"},{"w":"crop failure","p":"n.phr.","d":"when crops do not grow well enough to harvest","c":"作物歉收","s":"A crop failure can push food prices up quickly, and poor families then have to spend more on rice and vegetables.","t":"作物歉收可能讓食物價格迅速上漲,而貧窮家庭就得花更多錢在米和蔬菜上。"},{"w":"yield","p":"n.","d":"the amount of crops a farm produces","c":"產量;收成","s":"The rice yield fell sharply this year because of the heat, so the price of a bowl of rice went up.","t":"由於高溫,今年稻米的產量大幅下降,所以一碗飯的價格上漲了。"},{"w":"heat-related","p":"adj.","d":"caused by very hot weather","c":"與高溫相關的","s":"Doctors reported more heat-related illnesses this summer, and most of the patients were outdoor workers or elderly people.","t":"醫生回報今年夏天與高溫相關的疾病增加了,而大多數病人是戶外工作者或年長者。"},{"w":"malaria","p":"n.","d":"a serious disease spread by mosquitoes","c":"瘧疾","s":"malaria used to be rare in the highlands of Kenya, but warmer weather now lets mosquitoes live there.","t":"瘧疾過去在肯亞高地很少見,但較暖的天氣現在讓蚊子能在那裡生存。"},{"w":"mosquito","p":"n.","d":"a small flying insect that bites people","c":"蚊子","s":"Every summer the city sprays areas where mosquito breed, because they can spread dengue fever.","t":"每年夏天市政府都會在蚊子繁殖的地方噴藥,因為牠們會傳播登革熱。"},{"w":"infectious","p":"adj.","d":"able to spread from one person to another","c":"傳染性的","s":"Floods can spread infectious diseases quickly, so health workers handed out clean water and medicine after the storm.","t":"洪水可能讓傳染性疾病迅速擴散,所以暴風雨過後衛生人員發放了乾淨的水和藥品。"},{"w":"refugee","p":"n.","d":"a person forced to leave their home or country","c":"難民","s":"Some experts believe that climate refugee will increase in the future, because rising seas and droughts make places unsafe.","t":"一些專家認為氣候難民未來會增加,因為上升的海平面和乾旱讓一些地方變得不安全。"},{"w":"displacement","p":"n.","d":"the forced movement of people from their homes","c":"流離失所;被迫遷移","s":"The floods caused the displacement of thousands of families, and many of them still live in temporary camps.","t":"這場洪水造成數千個家庭流離失所,其中許多人至今仍住在臨時營地。"},{"w":"migrant","p":"n.","d":"a person who moves to another place to find work or safety","c":"移民;移工","s":"Many migrant left their dry farms and moved to the city, but finding a job there was not easy.","t":"許多移民離開了他們乾旱的農地搬到城市,但在那裡找工作並不容易。"},{"w":"homeless","p":"adj.","d":"having no place to live","c":"無家可歸的","s":"The typhoon left hundreds of people homeless, so local temples opened their doors and offered free meals.","t":"颱風讓數百人無家可歸,所以當地廟宇敞開大門並提供免費餐點。"},{"w":"property","p":"n.","d":"buildings and land that someone owns","c":"房地產;財產","s":"property near the beach used to be very valuable, but buyers are now worried about flooding and rising seas.","t":"海灘附近的房地產過去非常值錢,但買家現在擔心淹水和海平面上升。"},{"w":"insurance","p":"n.","d":"an agreement to pay money if something is damaged or lost","c":"保險","s":"After three floods in five years, the company refused to sell insurance to homeowners in that area.","t":"五年內發生三次水災之後,這家公司拒絕賣保險給那個地區的屋主。"},{"w":"premium","p":"n.","d":"the amount paid regularly for insurance","c":"保費","s":"Our home insurance premium doubled this year, because the company now sees our street as a high-risk area.","t":"我們的房屋保險保費今年翻倍了,因為保險公司現在把我們這條街視為高風險地區。"},{"w":"damage","p":"n.","d":"physical harm that makes something less useful or valuable","c":"損害;損壞","s":"The storm caused serious damage to the school roof, so classes moved to the library for two weeks.","t":"暴風雨對學校屋頂造成了嚴重的損害,所以上課地點移到圖書館兩週。"},{"w":"poverty","p":"n.","d":"the state of being very poor","c":"貧窮","s":"Climate change can push families into poverty, because one bad harvest may take away a whole year's income.","t":"氣候變遷可能把家庭推向貧窮,因為一次歉收就可能奪走一整年的收入。"},{"w":"food security","p":"n.phr.","d":"having enough safe, healthy food to eat","c":"糧食安全","s":"Taiwan imports most of its wheat, so food security is an important topic when global harvests fail.","t":"台灣大部分的小麥都靠進口,所以當全球收成不佳時,糧食安全是一個重要的議題。"},{"w":"malnourished","p":"adj.","d":"weak or ill because of not eating enough healthy food","c":"營養不良的","s":"After two failed harvests, many children in the village were malnourished, so a charity started a free lunch programme.","t":"連續兩次歉收後,村裡許多孩子營養不良,所以一個慈善團體開始了免費午餐計畫。"},{"w":"wither","p":"v.","d":"to become dry and weak and start to die","c":"枯萎","s":"The vegetables in our garden began to wither in the heat, so my mother watered them twice a day.","t":"我們菜園裡的蔬菜在高溫中開始枯萎,所以我媽媽一天澆兩次水。"},{"w":"parched","p":"adj.","d":"very dry because of no rain","c":"乾裂的;焦乾的","s":"The fields were brown and parched after months without rain, and the cows had little grass to eat.","t":"幾個月沒下雨後,田地變得又黃又乾裂,牛群幾乎沒有草可吃。"},{"w":"desertification","p":"n.","d":"the process of land slowly becoming desert","c":"沙漠化","s":"desertification is spreading in northern China, so millions of trees have been planted to stop the sand.","t":"沙漠化正在中國北方擴散,所以已經種了數百萬棵樹來阻擋沙子。"},{"w":"algae","p":"n.","d":"very simple plants that grow in water","c":"藻類","s":"Warm water caused algae to grow quickly in the lake, and the fish died because there was not enough oxygen.","t":"溫暖的水讓湖中的藻類迅速生長,魚群因為氧氣不足而死亡。"},{"w":"range","p":"n.","d":"the area where a plant or animal lives","c":"分布範圍","s":"The range of this butterfly has moved two hundred kilometres north, because its old home has become too warm.","t":"這種蝴蝶的分布範圍已經向北移動了兩百公里,因為牠原本的家變得太熱了。"},{"w":"heat island","p":"n.phr.","d":"a city area much warmer than the countryside around it","c":"熱島","s":"The city centre is a heat island in summer, because concrete and cars trap heat even at night.","t":"市中心在夏天是一個熱島,因為混凝土和汽車即使在夜間也會困住熱能。"},{"w":"hardship","p":"n.","d":"a difficult situation, often without enough money or food","c":"苦難;困境","s":"The drought brought great hardship to farming families, but neighbours shared water and food to help each other.","t":"乾旱為務農家庭帶來極大的困境,但鄰居們分享水和食物互相幫助。"},{"w":"uninhabitable","p":"adj.","d":"not safe or suitable for people to live in","c":"不適合居住的","s":"Some scientists fear that parts of the Middle East could become uninhabitable in summer, because the heat will be too extreme.","t":"一些科學家擔心中東部分地區在夏天可能變得不適合居住,因為高溫將過於極端。"}]},{"unit":6,"theme":"Adaptation & Resilience 調適與韌性","cards":[{"w":"adaptation","p":"n.","d":"a change made to deal with new conditions","c":"調適;適應","s":"Climate adaptation includes simple steps like planting trees for shade, so it is not only about expensive engineering.","t":"氣候調適包括像種樹遮蔭這樣簡單的步驟,所以它不只是關於昂貴的工程。"},{"w":"resilient","p":"adj.","d":"able to recover quickly after something bad happens","c":"有韌性的;能迅速復原的","s":"The new hospital was designed to be resilient, so it can keep running even if the power goes out during a storm.","t":"新醫院被設計得很有韌性,所以即使暴風雨中停電也能持續運作。"},{"w":"seawall","p":"n.","d":"a strong wall built to stop the sea from flooding land","c":"海堤","s":"The town built a taller seawall along the beach, but some people say it ruined the view of the ocean.","t":"鎮上沿著海灘建了一道更高的海堤,但有些人說它破壞了海景。"},{"w":"levee","p":"n.","d":"a raised bank built beside a river to stop flooding","c":"河堤;防洪堤","s":"The levee along the river held back the water, so the neighbourhood stayed dry during the heavy rain.","t":"沿著河邊的河堤擋住了河水,所以這個社區在大雨期間保持乾燥。"},{"w":"embankment","p":"n.","d":"a wall of earth or stone that holds back water","c":"堤防;路堤","s":"Volunteers filled sandbags to make the embankment higher, and they worked through the night before the river peaked.","t":"志工們裝填沙包把堤防加高,他們在河水達到最高點前通宵工作。"},{"w":"floodgate","p":"n.","d":"a gate that controls the flow of water","c":"水閘門","s":"Workers closed the floodgate before the typhoon arrived, so the seawater could not flow into the canal.","t":"工人在颱風來臨前關閉了水閘門,所以海水無法流進運河。"},{"w":"drainage","p":"n.","d":"the system that carries away extra water","c":"排水(系統)","s":"The old drainage system cannot handle today's heavy rain, so the city is digging wider pipes under the streets.","t":"舊的排水系統無法應付現今的大雨,所以市政府正在街道下方挖設更寬的管線。"},{"w":"reservoir","p":"n.","d":"a large lake used to store water","c":"水庫","s":"The water in the reservoir dropped to ten percent, so the government asked everyone to take shorter showers.","t":"水庫的水位降到百分之十,所以政府要求大家縮短淋浴時間。"},{"w":"irrigation","p":"n.","d":"supplying water to land so crops can grow","c":"灌溉","s":"Drip irrigation gives water directly to plant roots, so farmers can grow food while using much less water.","t":"滴水灌溉直接把水送到植物根部,所以農夫可以用少得多的水種出糧食。"},{"w":"irrigate","p":"v.","d":"to supply water to land through pipes or channels","c":"灌溉","s":"The farmers irrigate their fields at night now, because less water evaporates when the sun is down.","t":"農夫們現在在夜間灌溉田地,因為太陽下山後蒸發的水較少。"},{"w":"drought-resistant","p":"adj.","d":"able to grow well with little water","c":"耐旱的","s":"Scientists developed drought-resistant rice, so farmers can still get a harvest when the rains come late.","t":"科學家研發出耐旱稻米,所以即使雨水來得晚,農夫仍然可以有收成。"},{"w":"early warning system","p":"n.phr.","d":"a system that tells people about danger before it arrives","c":"預警系統","s":"The new early warning system sends text messages before floods, so families have time to move to higher ground.","t":"新的預警系統會在淹水前發送簡訊,讓家庭有時間移往地勢較高處。"},{"w":"elevate","p":"v.","d":"to raise something to a higher position","c":"抬高;架高","s":"Many families elevate their houses on concrete posts, so floodwater can pass underneath without entering the rooms.","t":"許多家庭把房子架高在混凝土柱上,讓洪水可以從下方流過而不會進到房間。"},{"w":"stilts","p":"n.","d":"tall posts that hold a building above the ground or water","c":"高腳柱;支柱","s":"The fishermen's houses stand on stilts above the water, so they stay safe when the tide is unusually high.","t":"漁民的房子立在水面上的高腳柱上,所以即使潮水異常高漲也能保持安全。"},{"w":"rainwater","p":"n.","d":"water that has fallen as rain","c":"雨水","s":"Our school collects rainwater from the roof in large tanks, and we use it to water the garden and flush toilets.","t":"我們學校用大水塔收集屋頂的雨水,用來澆花和沖馬桶。"},{"w":"desalination","p":"n.","d":"the process of removing salt from sea water","c":"海水淡化","s":"The island built a desalination plant because its wells were drying up, but the drinking water is now more expensive.","t":"這座島建了一座海水淡化廠,因為島上的水井快要乾涸,但飲用水現在變得更貴了。"},{"w":"shade","p":"n.","d":"an area that is darker and cooler because the sun cannot reach it","c":"陰涼處;遮蔭","s":"The city planted trees along the bus stops, so passengers can wait in the shade on hot afternoons.","t":"市政府在公車站旁種了樹,讓乘客在炎熱的下午可以在陰涼處等車。"},{"w":"reforestation","p":"n.","d":"planting trees in an area where forests were cut down","c":"重新造林","s":"The reforestation project has planted a million trees, and the hills now hold rainwater instead of sliding down.","t":"這項重新造林計畫已種下一百萬棵樹,現在山丘能留住雨水而不會崩塌。"},{"w":"replant","p":"v.","d":"to plant again","c":"重新種植;補種","s":"After the fire, students helped replant young trees on the hill, and they return every year to check them.","t":"火災之後,學生們幫忙在山坡上補種小樹,而且他們每年都會回去查看。"},{"w":"green roof","p":"n.phr.","d":"a roof covered with plants","c":"綠屋頂","s":"Our library has a green roof full of plants, so the building stays cooler and absorbs heavy rain.","t":"我們的圖書館有一座長滿植物的綠屋頂,所以建築物保持較涼爽,也能吸收大雨。"},{"w":"ventilation","p":"n.","d":"the movement of fresh air through a room or building","c":"通風","s":"Good ventilation keeps classrooms cooler without air-conditioning, so the new school has large windows on both sides.","t":"良好的通風能讓教室在不開冷氣的情況下保持涼爽,所以新學校兩側都有大窗戶。"},{"w":"air-conditioning","p":"n.","d":"a system that keeps the air in a building cool","c":"空調;冷氣","s":"Many families cannot afford air-conditioning, so heatwaves are especially dangerous for poor and elderly people.","t":"許多家庭負擔不起冷氣,所以熱浪對貧窮和年長者特別危險。"},{"w":"cooling centre","p":"n.phr.","d":"a public place where people can escape extreme heat","c":"避暑中心;降溫中心","s":"The library became a cooling centre during the heatwave, and older residents spent the afternoon there reading newspapers.","t":"熱浪期間圖書館成了避暑中心,年長居民在那裡看報紙度過下午。"},{"w":"preparedness","p":"n.","d":"the state of being ready for an emergency","c":"準備就緒;防備","s":"Disaster preparedness starts at home, so every family should have a bag with water, a torch and medicine.","t":"災害防備從家裡開始,所以每個家庭都應該準備一個裝有水、手電筒和藥品的包包。"},{"w":"contingency plan","p":"n.phr.","d":"a plan for what to do if something goes wrong","c":"應變計畫","s":"The festival organisers had a contingency plan for bad weather, so the concert moved indoors when the storm came.","t":"活動主辦單位有針對惡劣天氣的應變計畫,所以暴風雨來時音樂會就移到室內舉行。"},{"w":"retrofit","p":"v.","d":"to add new parts to an old building or machine","c":"翻修改裝;加裝","s":"The city will retrofit old apartment buildings with better insulation, so residents can stay cool and pay less for electricity.","t":"市政府將為老舊公寓大樓加裝更好的隔熱設備,讓居民可以保持涼爽並少付電費。"},{"w":"flood-prone","p":"adj.","d":"likely to flood","c":"易淹水的","s":"New homes should not be built in flood-prone areas, but land there is cheap, so developers keep building.","t":"新房子不應該蓋在易淹水的地區,但那裡的土地便宜,所以開發商一直在蓋。"},{"w":"zoning","p":"n.","d":"rules about how land in an area may be used","c":"土地分區管制","s":"The new zoning rules stop building near the river, and the land will become a park that can safely flood.","t":"新的土地分區規定禁止在河邊建房,這塊地將變成一座可以安全淹水的公園。"},{"w":"managed retreat","p":"n.phr.","d":"a planned move of people away from dangerous coastal areas","c":"有計畫的撤退(遷移)","s":"The village chose managed retreat instead of building a huge wall, so the families moved inland with government help.","t":"這個村莊選擇了有計畫的撤退,而不是建造巨大的牆,所以這些家庭在政府協助下遷往內陸。"},{"w":"stockpile","p":"v.","d":"to collect and store a large supply of something","c":"儲備;囤積","s":"Before the typhoon season, the town stockpile rice, water and medicine, so nobody went hungry when the roads closed.","t":"颱風季前,鎮上儲備了米、水和藥品,所以道路封閉時沒有人挨餓。"}]},{"unit":7,"theme":"Mitigation, Energy & Climate Policy 減緩、能源與氣候政策","cards":[{"w":"mitigation","p":"n.","d":"actions that reduce how bad something is","c":"減緩;緩解","s":"Climate mitigation means cutting emissions, while adaptation means preparing for the changes that are already coming.","t":"氣候減緩指的是減少排放,而調適則是為已經到來的變化做準備。"},{"w":"renewable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be replaced naturally, like sun and wind","c":"可再生的","s":"Taiwan wants more renewable energy, so wind farms are being built off the west coast.","t":"台灣希望有更多可再生能源,所以正在西部外海興建風場。"},{"w":"wind turbine","p":"n.phr.","d":"a tall machine that uses wind to make electricity","c":"風力發電機","s":"Each wind turbine off the coast can power thousands of homes, but fishermen worry about losing their fishing areas.","t":"外海的每一座風力發電機都能供應數千戶家庭用電,但漁民擔心失去他們的漁場。"},{"w":"solar panel","p":"n.phr.","d":"a flat device that turns sunlight into electricity","c":"太陽能板","s":"My uncle put solar panel on his roof, and now his electricity bill is almost zero in summer.","t":"我叔叔在他家屋頂裝了太陽能板,現在他夏天的電費幾乎是零。"},{"w":"hydropower","p":"n.","d":"electricity made from moving water","c":"水力發電","s":"hydropower provides clean electricity, but dams can also flood valleys and change the life of a river.","t":"水力發電提供潔淨的電力,但水壩也可能淹沒山谷並改變河流的生態。"},{"w":"geothermal","p":"adj.","d":"using heat from inside the Earth","c":"地熱的","s":"Iceland uses geothermal energy to heat most of its homes, because hot water lies just under the ground.","t":"冰島使用地熱能源為大部分的住家供暖,因為熱水就在地底下不遠處。"},{"w":"biofuel","p":"n.","d":"fuel made from plants or animal waste","c":"生質燃料","s":"Some airlines are testing biofuel made from used cooking oil, but there is not enough of it for every plane.","t":"一些航空公司正在測試用廢食用油製成的生質燃料,但數量還不夠供應每架飛機。"},{"w":"electric vehicle","p":"n.phr.","d":"a car or scooter that runs on a battery","c":"電動車","s":"My father bought an electric vehicle last year, and he charges it at home every night after work.","t":"我爸爸去年買了一輛電動車,他每天下班後晚上都在家充電。"},{"w":"battery","p":"n.","d":"a device that stores electricity","c":"電池","s":"Large battery can store solar power during the day, so homes can still use clean energy at night.","t":"大型電池可以在白天儲存太陽能,讓家庭在夜間仍然能使用潔淨能源。"},{"w":"grid","p":"n.","d":"the network of power lines that delivers electricity","c":"電網","s":"The power grid could not handle the demand during the heatwave, so some areas had blackouts in the evening.","t":"熱浪期間電網無法負荷用電需求,所以有些地區在傍晚停電。"},{"w":"insulation","p":"n.","d":"material that stops heat from getting in or out","c":"隔熱(材料)","s":"Good roof insulation keeps the top floor cooler in summer, so the family uses the air-conditioner much less.","t":"良好的屋頂隔熱能讓頂樓在夏天保持涼爽,所以這家人使用冷氣的次數大幅減少。"},{"w":"energy-efficient","p":"adj.","d":"using less energy to do the same job","c":"節能的","s":"We replaced our old fridge with an energy-efficient model, and our monthly electricity bill dropped quite a lot.","t":"我們把舊冰箱換成節能型號,每月的電費也下降了不少。"},{"w":"recycle","p":"v.","d":"to treat used things so they can be used again","c":"回收","s":"Our class tries to recycle every bottle and can, and we use the money from the recycling centre for a class trip.","t":"我們班盡量回收每一個瓶子和罐子,並用從回收中心換來的錢去校外旅行。"},{"w":"carbon tax","p":"n.phr.","d":"a charge on fuels that produce carbon","c":"碳稅","s":"The government introduced a carbon tax on big factories, so many companies started to look for cleaner ways to work.","t":"政府對大型工廠開徵碳稅,所以許多公司開始尋找更乾淨的運作方式。"},{"w":"pledge","p":"n.","d":"a serious promise","c":"承諾;保證","s":"Many countries made a pledge to reach net zero, but their actions so far are not enough to meet it.","t":"許多國家做出了達到淨零的承諾,但它們到目前為止的行動還不足以實現它。"},{"w":"summit","p":"n.","d":"an important meeting between leaders","c":"高峰會","s":"World leaders met at the climate summit in November, but they could not agree on how much money to give poorer nations.","t":"世界領袖們在十一月的氣候高峰會上會面,但他們無法就該給較貧窮國家多少資金達成共識。"},{"w":"delegate","p":"n.","d":"a person sent to a meeting to represent others","c":"代表","s":"The young delegate from a Pacific island gave an emotional speech, and many people in the room started crying.","t":"來自一座太平洋島嶼的年輕代表發表了一場動人的演說,會場上許多人都哭了。"},{"w":"accord","p":"n.","d":"an official agreement between countries","c":"協定;協議","s":"The Paris accord was signed by almost every country, but each nation decides its own plan to cut emissions.","t":"《巴黎協定》幾乎每個國家都簽署了,但每個國家自行決定減排計畫。"},{"w":"commitment","p":"n.","d":"a promise to do something","c":"承諾;投入","s":"The company made a commitment to use only green electricity, so it signed a long contract with a wind farm.","t":"這家公司承諾只使用綠電,所以它與一座風場簽訂了長期合約。"},{"w":"ratify","p":"v.","d":"to make an agreement official by signing or voting","c":"正式批准","s":"Parliament voted to ratify the climate agreement, and the new law will start next January.","t":"國會投票正式批准這項氣候協議,新法將於明年一月開始實施。"},{"w":"carbon-neutral","p":"adj.","d":"adding no extra carbon to the atmosphere overall","c":"碳中和的","s":"Our school wants to become carbon-neutral by 2030, so we are planting trees and putting solar panels on the gym.","t":"我們學校希望在2030年前達到碳中和,所以我們正在種樹並在體育館上裝設太陽能板。"},{"w":"nuclear","p":"adj.","d":"using energy from splitting atoms","c":"核能的","s":"nuclear power produces very little carbon, but many people worry about accidents and how to store the waste.","t":"核能發電產生的碳非常少,但許多人擔心意外事故以及如何貯存廢料。"},{"w":"activist","p":"n.","d":"a person who works to bring political or social change","c":"社運人士;行動者","s":"The young climate activist spoke at the United Nations, and her speech inspired students in many countries.","t":"這位年輕的氣候行動者在聯合國發表演說,她的演講激勵了許多國家的學生。"},{"w":"protest","p":"n.","d":"a public event where people show they disagree","c":"抗議(活動)","s":"Thousands of students joined the climate protest on Friday, and they carried signs asking leaders to act now.","t":"數千名學生參加了星期五的氣候抗議活動,他們舉著標語要求領袖們立即行動。"},{"w":"greenwashing","p":"n.","d":"making a product seem better for nature than it really is","c":"漂綠","s":"The ad showed trees and rivers, but the company still burned coal, so critics called it greenwashing.","t":"這則廣告展示了樹木和河流,但這家公司仍在燒煤,所以批評者稱之為漂綠。"},{"w":"carbon capture","p":"n.phr.","d":"technology that catches carbon dioxide and stores it","c":"碳捕捉","s":"The power plant is testing carbon capture to trap its emissions, but the technology is still very expensive.","t":"這座發電廠正在測試碳捕捉以收集其排放,但這項技術仍然非常昂貴。"},{"w":"public transport","p":"n.phr.","d":"buses and trains that everyone can use","c":"大眾運輸","s":"If more people took public transport instead of driving, the city would have less traffic and cleaner air.","t":"如果更多人搭乘大眾運輸而不開車,城市就會有更少的車流和更乾淨的空氣。"},{"w":"compost","p":"v.","d":"to turn food and garden waste into natural fertiliser","c":"堆肥","s":"Our family started to compost vegetable scraps in the garden, and now we throw away much less rubbish.","t":"我們家開始在花園裡把菜渣拿來堆肥,現在我們丟的垃圾少多了。"}]},{"unit":8,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 1 (unprecedented – correlate)","cards":[{"w":"unprecedented","p":"adj.","d":"never happened before","c":"前所未有的","s":"The summer of 2023 brought unprecedented heat to many countries, and records that had stood for decades were broken.","t":"2023年夏天為許多國家帶來前所未有的高溫,保持了數十年的紀錄紛紛被打破。"},{"w":"profound","p":"adj.","d":"very great or serious","c":"深遠的;深刻的","s":"Rising seas will have a profound effect on island nations, so their leaders are asking the world for urgent help.","t":"海平面上升將對島國造成深遠的影響,所以它們的領袖正在向世界請求緊急協助。"},{"w":"pivotal","p":"adj.","d":"very important for what happens next","c":"關鍵的","s":"The next ten years will be pivotal for the climate, because decisions made now will affect the planet for centuries.","t":"未來十年對氣候將是關鍵的,因為現在所做的決定將影響地球好幾個世紀。"},{"w":"curb","p":"v.","d":"to control or limit something bad","c":"抑制;控制","s":"The new rules aim to curb air pollution from factories, but some owners say the changes are too expensive.","t":"新規定的目的是抑制工廠的空氣污染,但有些業主說這些改變太昂貴了。"},{"w":"tackle","p":"v.","d":"to deal with a difficult problem","c":"處理;應對","s":"No single country can tackle climate change alone, so nations must share their technology, ideas and money.","t":"沒有任何單一國家能獨自應對氣候變遷,所以各國必須分享它們的技術、想法和資金。"},{"w":"combat","p":"v.","d":"to try to stop something harmful","c":"對抗;打擊","s":"The city planted thousands of street trees to combat rising temperatures, and some streets are now two degrees cooler.","t":"市政府種了數千棵行道樹來對抗上升的氣溫,有些街道現在涼了兩度。"},{"w":"foster","p":"v.","d":"to help something develop","c":"促進;培養","s":"The teacher wants to foster a love of nature in her students, so she takes the class to the wetlands every month.","t":"這位老師想培養學生對大自然的熱愛,所以她每個月都帶全班去濕地。"},{"w":"bolster","p":"v.","d":"to make something stronger","c":"加強;支撐","s":"The government will bolster the river banks with stone, because last year's flood almost broke through.","t":"政府將用石頭加強河岸,因為去年的洪水差點沖破堤防。"},{"w":"hinder","p":"v.","d":"to make it difficult for something to happen","c":"阻礙","s":"Heavy rain hinder the rescue work, but the teams kept searching for missing people all night.","t":"大雨阻礙了救援工作,但救難隊仍整夜持續搜尋失蹤者。"},{"w":"impede","p":"v.","d":"to slow down or block progress","c":"妨礙;阻止","s":"Fallen trees impede traffic on the main road, so ambulances had to take a much longer route.","t":"倒下的樹木妨礙了主要道路的交通,所以救護車不得不繞一條更遠的路。"},{"w":"jeopardise","p":"v.","d":"to put something in danger","c":"危及;使陷入危險","s":"Warmer seas could jeopardise the fishing industry, and many coastal families would lose their main income.","t":"較暖的海水可能危及漁業,許多沿海家庭將失去他們主要的收入。"},{"w":"compromise","p":"n.","d":"an agreement where each side gives up something","c":"妥協;折衷","s":"The two groups reached a compromise after long talks, so the wind farm will be built further from the fishing area.","t":"兩個團體在長時間協商後達成妥協,所以風場將建在離漁場更遠的地方。"},{"w":"escalate","p":"v.","d":"to become more serious or bigger","c":"升級;加劇","s":"The water dispute between the two farms began to escalate, so the village leader invited them to a meeting.","t":"兩座農場之間的用水糾紛開始加劇,所以村長邀請他們來開會。"},{"w":"surge","p":"n.","d":"a sudden large increase","c":"激增;暴增","s":"There was a surge in electricity use during the heatwave, and the power company asked people to save energy.","t":"熱浪期間用電量激增,電力公司要求民眾節約能源。"},{"w":"plummet","p":"v.","d":"to fall suddenly and by a large amount","c":"暴跌;驟降","s":"Fish numbers plummet after the water became too warm, so the fishermen had to stay in port for weeks.","t":"海水變得太暖之後魚群數量驟降,所以漁民不得不在港口停留好幾週。"},{"w":"soar","p":"v.","d":"to rise very quickly to a high level","c":"飆升;猛增","s":"Vegetable prices soar after the typhoon damaged the farms, so my mother bought frozen vegetables instead.","t":"颱風損壞農田後菜價飆升,所以我媽媽改買冷凍蔬菜。"},{"w":"proliferate","p":"v.","d":"to increase quickly in number","c":"激增;迅速增加","s":"Electric scooters have proliferate in Taipei, and charging stations now appear on almost every street.","t":"電動機車在台北迅速增加,現在幾乎每條街上都有充電站。"},{"w":"amplify","p":"v.","d":"to make something stronger or more serious","c":"放大;增強","s":"Climate change can amplify natural dangers, so a normal storm may now cause much more damage.","t":"氣候變遷可能放大自然災害的危險,所以一場普通的暴風雨現在可能造成更多損害。"},{"w":"magnify","p":"v.","d":"to make something seem or become bigger","c":"擴大;放大","s":"Poor building rules magnify the damage from earthquakes and floods, so experts want stricter checks.","t":"不良的建築規範擴大了地震和洪水造成的損害,所以專家希望實施更嚴格的檢查。"},{"w":"trajectory","p":"n.","d":"the path or direction of development","c":"軌跡;發展趨勢","s":"On the current trajectory, the world will warm by almost three degrees, but faster action could change this path.","t":"照目前的發展趨勢,世界將升溫將近三度,但更快的行動可以改變這條路徑。"},{"w":"threshold","p":"n.","d":"the level at which something starts to happen","c":"門檻;臨界點","s":"Once the temperature passes a certain threshold, coral begins to die, and recovery can take many years.","t":"一旦溫度超過某個臨界點,珊瑚就開始死亡,而復原可能需要許多年。"},{"w":"baseline","p":"n.","d":"a starting point used for comparison","c":"基準線","s":"The scientists used 1990 as the baseline, so every later measurement could be compared with that year.","t":"科學家們以1990年作為基準線,讓之後的每個測量值都可以與那一年比較。"},{"w":"projection","p":"n.","d":"an estimate of what will happen in the future","c":"預測;推估","s":"The latest projection shows that sea levels could rise by one metre, but this depends on how fast ice melts.","t":"最新的推估顯示海平面可能上升一公尺,但這取決於冰融化的速度。"},{"w":"variable","p":"n.","d":"a factor that can change","c":"變數;變因","s":"Rainfall is an important variable in the study, because it affects both crop growth and river levels.","t":"降雨量是這項研究中的一個重要變數,因為它同時影響作物生長和河川水位。"},{"w":"correlate","p":"v.","d":"to have a close connection","c":"相關;相互關聯","s":"Hospital visits correlate closely with hot days, so doctors prepare extra beds when a heatwave is forecast.","t":"醫院就診人數與炎熱天數密切相關,所以每當預報熱浪,醫生就會準備額外病床。"}]},{"unit":9,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 2 (discrepancy – endorse)","cards":[{"w":"discrepancy","p":"n.","d":"a difference between things that should match","c":"差異;出入","s":"There was a discrepancy between the two temperature records, so the team checked the instruments again.","t":"兩份溫度紀錄之間有出入,所以團隊再次檢查了儀器。"},{"w":"consistently","p":"adv.","d":"always in the same way","c":"一貫地;始終","s":"The island has consistently recorded higher temperatures since 2000, and this pattern worries local farmers.","t":"這座島自2000年以來始終記錄到較高的氣溫,這個模式讓當地農民很擔心。"},{"w":"notably","p":"adv.","d":"especially; in a way that is worth noticing","c":"尤其;顯著地","s":"Many countries have cut emissions, notably the UK, which has closed almost all of its coal power plants.","t":"許多國家已經減少排放,尤其是英國,它已經關閉了幾乎所有的燃煤發電廠。"},{"w":"predominantly","p":"adv.","d":"mainly; mostly","c":"主要地;大多","s":"The region is predominantly agricultural, so long dry seasons hurt almost every family's income there.","t":"這個地區主要以農業為主,所以漫長的乾季幾乎影響當地每個家庭的收入。"},{"w":"substantially","p":"adv.","d":"by a large amount","c":"大幅地;相當多地","s":"The cost of solar panels has fallen substantially in ten years, so more families can now afford them.","t":"太陽能板的成本在十年內大幅下降,所以現在更多家庭負擔得起。"},{"w":"marginal","p":"adj.","d":"very small and not important","c":"微小的;邊際的","s":"Changing light bulbs makes only a marginal difference, but bigger changes like better buses can help a lot.","t":"換燈泡只帶來微小的差異,但像改善公車這樣較大的改變可以幫助很多。"},{"w":"negligible","p":"adj.","d":"so small that it is not important","c":"微不足道的","s":"The extra cost of the green design was negligible, and the building saves a lot of money on energy every year.","t":"綠色設計的額外成本微不足道,而這棟建築每年在能源上節省很多錢。"},{"w":"drastic","p":"adj.","d":"extreme and having a strong effect","c":"激烈的;大幅的","s":"Scientists say we need drastic cuts in emissions, because small changes will not stop dangerous warming.","t":"科學家說我們需要大幅削減排放,因為小小的改變無法阻止危險的暖化。"},{"w":"severe","p":"adj.","d":"very serious or bad","c":"嚴重的;劇烈的","s":"The farm suffered severe damage in the storm, but the family received help from neighbours and the government.","t":"這座農場在暴風雨中受到嚴重的損害,但這家人得到鄰居和政府的幫助。"},{"w":"imminent","p":"adj.","d":"going to happen very soon","c":"即將發生的;迫在眉睫的","s":"The warning said a flood was imminent, so families quickly moved their belongings to the second floor.","t":"警報說洪水即將發生,所以家家戶戶趕緊把財物搬到二樓。"},{"w":"feasible","p":"adj.","d":"possible and practical to do","c":"可行的","s":"Building a wall around the whole island is not feasible, so the government is looking for cheaper ideas.","t":"在整座島周圍築牆並不可行,所以政府正在尋找較便宜的辦法。"},{"w":"viable","p":"adj.","d":"able to work successfully","c":"可行的;能成功的","s":"Electric buses are now a viable choice for small towns, because batteries have become cheaper and last longer.","t":"電動公車現在對小鎮來說是可行的選擇,因為電池變得更便宜也更耐用。"},{"w":"pragmatic","p":"adj.","d":"dealing with problems in a practical way","c":"務實的","s":"The mayor took a pragmatic approach to flooding, and she fixed the drains before planning any big projects.","t":"市長以務實的方式處理淹水問題,在規劃任何大型工程之前先修好了排水溝。"},{"w":"ambitious","p":"adj.","d":"needing a lot of effort to achieve","c":"雄心勃勃的;遠大的","s":"The country set an ambitious goal of zero emissions by 2040, but it has not explained how it will pay for it.","t":"這個國家訂下2040年零排放的遠大目標,但它還沒有說明要如何支付費用。"},{"w":"stringent","p":"adj.","d":"very strict","c":"嚴格的","s":"The European Union has stringent rules on car emissions, so companies must build cleaner engines to sell there.","t":"歐盟對汽車排放有嚴格的規定,所以公司必須製造更乾淨的引擎才能在那裡銷售。"},{"w":"lenient","p":"adj.","d":"not strict enough","c":"寬鬆的;寬容的","s":"Critics say the punishment for illegal dumping is too lenient, so some companies simply pay the fine and continue.","t":"批評者說非法傾倒的處罰太寬鬆,所以有些公司只是繳罰款然後繼續做。"},{"w":"comprehensive","p":"adj.","d":"including everything that is needed","c":"全面的;綜合的","s":"The city published a comprehensive plan for heatwaves, and it covers schools, hospitals, buses and parks.","t":"市政府發布了一份全面的熱浪應對計畫,內容涵蓋學校、醫院、公車和公園。"},{"w":"holistic","p":"adj.","d":"looking at the whole situation, not just parts","c":"全面的;整體的","s":"Experts call for a holistic approach to water, so cities should think about rain, rivers and drinking water together.","t":"專家呼籲對水資源採取整體的方法,所以城市應該把雨水、河川和飲用水放在一起考慮。"},{"w":"equitable","p":"adj.","d":"fair to everyone","c":"公平的;公正的","s":"The climate fund must be equitable, because the poorest countries suffer the most but caused the least pollution.","t":"氣候基金必須是公平的,因為最貧窮的國家受害最深,卻造成最少的污染。"},{"w":"disproportionate","p":"adj.","d":"too large or too small compared with something else","c":"不成比例的","s":"Heatwaves have a disproportionate effect on old people, so nurses visit those who live alone during hot weather.","t":"熱浪對老年人造成不成比例的影響,所以天氣炎熱時護理師會去探訪獨居者。"},{"w":"fragile","p":"adj.","d":"easily broken or damaged","c":"脆弱的","s":"Mountain ecosystems are very fragile, and even a small rise in temperature can change which plants survive there.","t":"山區生態系非常脆弱,即使氣溫小幅上升也可能改變哪些植物能在那裡存活。"},{"w":"prioritise","p":"v.","d":"to treat something as more important than other things","c":"優先處理","s":"The town decided to prioritise flood defences, so the new sports stadium will have to wait a few years.","t":"鎮上決定優先處理防洪設施,所以新的運動場得等上幾年。"},{"w":"mobilise","p":"v.","d":"to organise people or resources for action","c":"動員","s":"The school managed to mobilise two hundred volunteers, and they cleaned the beach in just one morning.","t":"學校成功動員了兩百名志工,他們只花一個早上就清乾淨了海灘。"},{"w":"lobby","p":"v.","d":"to try to influence politicians","c":"遊說","s":"Oil companies lobby the government for years, so laws to cut emissions were delayed again and again.","t":"石油公司多年來一直遊說政府,所以減排法律一再被延遲。"},{"w":"endorse","p":"v.","d":"to publicly support something","c":"支持;背書","s":"Several famous athletes endorse the tree-planting campaign, and thousands of young fans signed up to help.","t":"幾位知名運動員公開支持植樹活動,數千名年輕粉絲報名參加。"}]},{"unit":10,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 3 (oppose – urgency)","cards":[{"w":"oppose","p":"v.","d":"to disagree with and try to stop something","c":"反對","s":"Local residents oppose the new airport, because it would destroy farmland and increase air pollution.","t":"當地居民反對興建新機場,因為它會破壞農地並增加空氣污染。"},{"w":"reconcile","p":"v.","d":"to find a way for two different ideas to exist together","c":"調和;使一致","s":"It is hard to reconcile economic growth with lower emissions, but some countries have managed to do both.","t":"要調和經濟成長與降低排放很困難,但有些國家已經成功做到兩者兼顧。"},{"w":"concession","p":"n.","d":"something you agree to give up in a discussion","c":"讓步","s":"Rich countries made a concession on climate funding, so the talks finally ended with an agreement.","t":"富國在氣候資金上做出讓步,所以談判最終以達成協議收場。"},{"w":"levy","p":"n.","d":"an official charge or tax","c":"徵收的稅;稅款","s":"The airport introduced a small levy on every flight, and the money is used to plant forests.","t":"機場對每個航班徵收一筆小額稅款,這筆錢被用來種植森林。"},{"w":"deploy","p":"v.","d":"to put something into use or action","c":"部署;運用","s":"The government will deploy more soldiers and boats to the coast, because a strong typhoon is on its way.","t":"政府將在沿海部署更多士兵和船隻,因為一個強烈颱風正在逼近。"},{"w":"invest","p":"v.","d":"to put money into something to get a benefit later","c":"投資","s":"The city decided to invest in bike lanes, and now many students ride to school instead of taking the bus.","t":"市政府決定投資興建自行車道,現在許多學生改騎單車上學而不搭公車。"},{"w":"expenditure","p":"n.","d":"the amount of money spent","c":"支出;花費","s":"Government expenditure on disaster recovery has doubled, so less money is left for schools and hospitals.","t":"政府在災後復原上的支出已經翻倍,所以留給學校和醫院的錢變少了。"},{"w":"affordable","p":"adj.","d":"cheap enough for most people to buy","c":"負擔得起的","s":"Electric scooters are now more affordable, so many young workers have changed from petrol models.","t":"電動機車現在更負擔得起,所以許多年輕上班族已經從汽油車款換過去了。"},{"w":"cost-effective","p":"adj.","d":"giving good results for the money spent","c":"符合成本效益的","s":"Planting mangroves is a cost-effective way to protect the coast, and it also creates homes for fish and birds.","t":"種植紅樹林是保護海岸符合成本效益的方法,同時也為魚類和鳥類創造棲息地。"},{"w":"interim","p":"adj.","d":"temporary, until something permanent is ready","c":"臨時的;過渡期的","s":"The families moved into interim housing after the flood, but they hope to return home before New Year.","t":"這些家庭在水災後搬進了臨時住所,但他們希望在新年前能回家。"},{"w":"transitional","p":"adj.","d":"happening while changing from one state to another","c":"過渡的;轉型的","s":"Natural gas is often called a transitional fuel, because it is cleaner than coal but still not truly clean.","t":"天然氣常被稱為過渡燃料,因為它比煤乾淨,但仍不是真正的潔淨能源。"},{"w":"obligation","p":"n.","d":"something you must do because of a law or promise","c":"義務;責任","s":"Rich nations have an obligation to help poorer ones, because they produced most of the carbon in the past.","t":"富國有義務幫助較貧窮的國家,因為它們過去製造了大部分的碳。"},{"w":"mandate","p":"n.","d":"an official order to do something","c":"命令;授權;規定","s":"The new mandate requires all new buildings to have solar panels, so builders are changing their designs.","t":"新的規定要求所有新建築都必須裝設太陽能板,所以建商正在修改設計。"},{"w":"binding","p":"adj.","d":"that must be obeyed by law","c":"具有約束力的","s":"The agreement is not legally binding, so countries cannot be punished if they miss their targets.","t":"這份協議在法律上不具約束力,所以各國即使未達目標也不會受到處罰。"},{"w":"enact","p":"v.","d":"to make a law","c":"制定(法律);頒布","s":"The government plans to enact a new climate law this year, and it will set limits for every industry.","t":"政府計畫今年制定一部新的氣候法,而它將為每個產業設定上限。"},{"w":"dissent","p":"n.","d":"strong disagreement with an official opinion","c":"異議;不同意見","s":"There was some dissent among the scientists, but most of them agreed that the data showed clear warming.","t":"科學家之間有一些異議,但他們大多數人都同意數據顯示出明顯的暖化。"},{"w":"denial","p":"n.","d":"refusing to accept that something is true","c":"否認;否定","s":"Climate denial is less common today, because people can see the effects of extreme weather with their own eyes.","t":"氣候否定論如今較不常見,因為人們能親眼看見極端天氣的影響。"},{"w":"credible","p":"adj.","d":"able to be believed or trusted","c":"可信的","s":"Students should use credible sources for their climate projects, so they should check who wrote each website.","t":"學生的氣候專題應該使用可信的資料來源,所以他們應該查看每個網站是誰寫的。"},{"w":"rigorous","p":"adj.","d":"very careful and thorough","c":"嚴謹的;嚴格的","s":"The study used rigorous methods, and other scientists were able to repeat it and get the same results.","t":"這項研究使用了嚴謹的方法,其他科學家也能重複實驗並得到相同結果。"},{"w":"robust","p":"adj.","d":"strong and unlikely to fail","c":"強健的;穩固的","s":"The city needs a robust water system, so it will not fail during the next long drought.","t":"這座城市需要一個穩固的供水系統,這樣在下一次長期乾旱時才不會失靈。"},{"w":"peer-reviewed","p":"adj.","d":"checked by other experts before being published","c":"經同儕審查的","s":"The report was based on peer-reviewed research, so the government took its warnings very seriously.","t":"這份報告是以經同儕審查的研究為基礎,所以政府非常認真看待其中的警告。"},{"w":"unanimous","p":"adj.","d":"agreed by everyone","c":"一致同意的","s":"The vote was unanimous, and every member of the student council supported the plan to ban plastic bottles.","t":"這次投票是全體一致同意,學生會的每位成員都支持禁用塑膠瓶的計畫。"},{"w":"contentious","p":"adj.","d":"likely to cause disagreement","c":"有爭議的","s":"Building a dam in the valley is a contentious issue, because it brings clean power but floods people's homes.","t":"在山谷中興建水壩是一個有爭議的議題,因為它帶來潔淨電力卻也淹沒了人們的家園。"},{"w":"pressing","p":"adj.","d":"needing to be dealt with now","c":"緊迫的;迫切的","s":"Clean water is the most pressing problem after the flood, so the army is bringing in large water tanks.","t":"乾淨的水是水災過後最迫切的問題,所以軍隊正在運來大型水箱。"},{"w":"urgency","p":"n.","d":"the need to act quickly","c":"緊迫性;急迫","s":"Young people speak about climate change with real urgency, because they will live with the results for the longest time.","t":"年輕人談論氣候變遷時帶著真切的急迫感,因為他們將承受後果最久。"}]},{"unit":11,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 4 (collective – underscore)","cards":[{"w":"collective","p":"adj.","d":"done by a group of people together","c":"集體的;共同的","s":"Climate change needs collective action, so even small efforts by millions of people can make a difference.","t":"氣候變遷需要集體行動,所以即使是數百萬人的小小努力也能帶來改變。"},{"w":"equity","p":"n.","d":"fairness and equal treatment","c":"公平;公正","s":"equity is an important part of climate policy, because poor families should not pay the highest price for change.","t":"公平是氣候政策的重要部分,因為貧窮家庭不應該為改變付出最高的代價。"},{"w":"justice","p":"n.","d":"fair treatment for everyone","c":"正義;公正","s":"Activists call for climate justice, because the people least responsible for emissions often suffer the most.","t":"行動者呼籲氣候正義,因為對排放責任最小的人往往受害最深。"},{"w":"burden","p":"n.","d":"a heavy duty or problem that someone must deal with","c":"負擔;重擔","s":"The cost of rebuilding after floods is a heavy burden for small towns, so they need support from the central government.","t":"水災後重建的費用對小鎮來說是沉重的負擔,所以它們需要中央政府的支援。"},{"w":"liability","p":"n.","d":"legal responsibility for something","c":"(法律)責任","s":"The court decided the company had liability for the oil spill, so it must pay to clean the beaches.","t":"法院判決這家公司對漏油事件負有法律責任,所以它必須出錢清理海灘。"},{"w":"cumulative","p":"adj.","d":"increasing by adding one thing after another","c":"累積的","s":"The cumulative effect of small changes is large, so turning off lights every day really does save energy over time.","t":"小小改變的累積效果很大,所以每天隨手關燈長期下來確實能節省能源。"},{"w":"incremental","p":"adj.","d":"happening in small steps","c":"逐步的;漸進的","s":"The company is making incremental changes to its factories, but critics say it needs to move much faster.","t":"這家公司正對工廠做逐步的改變,但批評者說它需要加快速度。"},{"w":"exponential","p":"adj.","d":"increasing faster and faster","c":"指數型的;急遽增加的","s":"The growth of solar power has been exponential, and it now produces more electricity than anyone expected.","t":"太陽能的成長呈指數型,現在它產生的電力比任何人預期的都多。"},{"w":"linear","p":"adj.","d":"changing at a steady rate","c":"線性的;直線的","s":"Sea level rise is not linear, so it may speed up suddenly if large ice sheets begin to break apart.","t":"海平面上升並非線性的,所以如果大型冰原開始崩解,它可能會突然加速。"},{"w":"variability","p":"n.","d":"the quality of changing often","c":"變化性;變異性","s":"Rainfall variability makes farming difficult, because farmers never know whether the season will be wet or dry.","t":"降雨的變化性讓務農變得困難,因為農夫永遠不知道這一季會是濕潤還是乾燥。"},{"w":"magnitude","p":"n.","d":"the great size or importance of something","c":"規模;重要性","s":"Few people understood the magnitude of the problem, so the government reacted too slowly at first.","t":"很少人理解這個問題的規模,所以政府一開始反應太慢。"},{"w":"scale","p":"n.","d":"the size or level of something","c":"規模","s":"The scale of the flood shocked everyone, and the water covered an area larger than the whole city.","t":"洪水的規模讓每個人都震驚,淹水範圍比整座城市還大。"},{"w":"extent","p":"n.","d":"how large or serious something is","c":"程度;範圍","s":"Satellites showed the extent of the ice loss, and the photos made the news around the world.","t":"衛星顯示了冰層流失的範圍,這些照片登上了全世界的新聞。"},{"w":"aggregate","p":"adj.","d":"formed by adding together several amounts","c":"總計的;合計的","s":"The aggregate cost of the storms was billions of dollars, so insurance companies have raised their prices.","t":"這些暴風雨總計的損失高達數十億美元,所以保險公司已經調漲了價格。"},{"w":"median","p":"adj.","d":"in the middle of a set of numbers","c":"中位數的","s":"The median temperature this June was the highest on record, and the hottest days were even worse.","t":"今年六月的中位數氣溫是有紀錄以來最高的,而最熱的幾天更糟。"},{"w":"quantify","p":"v.","d":"to measure something as a number","c":"量化","s":"It is difficult to quantify the value of a forest, because it gives us clean air, water and beauty.","t":"要量化一座森林的價值很困難,因為它給予我們乾淨的空氣、水和美景。"},{"w":"calculate","p":"v.","d":"to find an answer using numbers","c":"計算","s":"We used an app to calculate our family's carbon footprint, and we were surprised by how much came from flying.","t":"我們用一個應用程式計算全家的碳足跡,很驚訝有那麼多來自搭飛機。"},{"w":"gauge","p":"v.","d":"to judge or measure something","c":"評估;估量","s":"It is hard to gauge public opinion on the new tax, so the city will hold online surveys next month.","t":"很難評估民眾對新稅的看法,所以市政府下個月將舉辦線上調查。"},{"w":"outline","p":"v.","d":"to describe the main points of something","c":"概述;簡述","s":"The minister outline the new energy plan on TV, but she did not explain how much it would cost.","t":"部長在電視上概述了新的能源計畫,但她沒有說明它會花多少錢。"},{"w":"elaborate","p":"v.","d":"to give more details","c":"詳細說明","s":"The reporter asked the scientist to elaborate on her research, so she explained how the ice samples were collected.","t":"記者請這位科學家詳細說明她的研究,所以她解釋了冰芯樣本是如何採集的。"},{"w":"articulate","p":"v.","d":"to express ideas clearly","c":"清楚表達","s":"The student was able to articulate her worries about the future, and the audience listened carefully.","t":"這位學生能夠清楚表達她對未來的擔憂,觀眾都仔細聆聽。"},{"w":"convey","p":"v.","d":"to communicate an idea or feeling","c":"傳達","s":"The photo of the thin polar bear convey the problem better than any graph, so it was shared millions of times.","t":"那張瘦弱北極熊的照片比任何圖表都更能傳達問題,所以它被分享了數百萬次。"},{"w":"depict","p":"v.","d":"to show something in a picture or story","c":"描繪","s":"The film depict a future city under water, and many viewers left the cinema feeling worried.","t":"這部電影描繪了一座被水淹沒的未來城市,許多觀眾離開電影院時心情沉重。"},{"w":"portray","p":"v.","d":"to describe or show someone or something in a certain way","c":"描寫;刻劃","s":"The news often portray farmers as victims, but many of them are also finding smart ways to adapt.","t":"新聞常常把農民描寫成受害者,但他們之中許多人也在找尋聰明的調適方法。"},{"w":"underscore","p":"v.","d":"to emphasise that something is important","c":"強調;凸顯","s":"The recent floods underscore the need for better drains, and the city council finally agreed to spend more money.","t":"最近的水災凸顯了改善排水系統的必要,市議會終於同意投入更多經費。"}]},{"unit":12,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 5 (reiterate – impartial)","cards":[{"w":"reiterate","p":"v.","d":"to say something again for emphasis","c":"重申","s":"The president reiterate her promise to close the coal plants, but she did not give a date.","t":"總統重申了她關閉燃煤電廠的承諾,但她沒有給出日期。"},{"w":"ascribe","p":"v.","d":"to say that something is caused by a certain thing","c":"把…歸因於","s":"Scientists ascribe most of the recent warming to human activity, and they have strong data to support this.","t":"科學家把近年大部分的暖化歸因於人類活動,而且他們有有力的數據支持。"},{"w":"arise","p":"v.","d":"to begin to happen or exist","c":"出現;產生","s":"New problems arose when the river dried up, so the farmers had to share water more carefully.","t":"河川乾涸時新的問題出現了,所以農夫們必須更謹慎地分配用水。"},{"w":"originate","p":"v.","d":"to begin or come from somewhere","c":"起源;源自","s":"Most typhoons that hit Taiwan originate over the warm Pacific Ocean, and warmer water makes them stronger.","t":"大多數侵襲台灣的颱風都源自溫暖的太平洋,而較暖的海水讓它們變得更強。"},{"w":"entail","p":"v.","d":"to involve something as a necessary part","c":"需要;牽涉","s":"Moving the whole village would entail huge costs, so the leaders are looking at other options first.","t":"遷移整個村莊將需要龐大的費用,所以領袖們先考慮其他選項。"},{"w":"necessitate","p":"v.","d":"to make something necessary","c":"使成為必要","s":"Rising sea levels will necessitate new building rules, and older houses near the beach may have to be raised.","t":"海平面上升將使新的建築規範成為必要,而海邊較舊的房子可能必須架高。"},{"w":"warrant","p":"v.","d":"to make an action seem right or necessary","c":"使…有必要;值得","s":"The danger was serious enough to warrant an evacuation, so the police went from door to door.","t":"危險嚴重到有必要進行撤離,所以警察挨家挨戶通知。"},{"w":"encompass","p":"v.","d":"to include many different things","c":"包含;涵蓋","s":"The new course will encompass science, economics and history, so students can see climate change from many angles.","t":"新課程將涵蓋科學、經濟和歷史,讓學生能從許多角度看待氣候變遷。"},{"w":"embody","p":"v.","d":"to be a clear example of an idea","c":"體現;代表","s":"The green school building embody the idea of living with nature, and visitors come from all over Asia to see it.","t":"這棟綠色校舍體現了與自然共存的理念,來自亞洲各地的訪客都來參觀。"},{"w":"exemplify","p":"v.","d":"to be a typical example of something","c":"作為…的典範","s":"Copenhagen exemplify how a city can cut emissions, because most people there cycle to work.","t":"哥本哈根是城市如何減少排放的典範,因為那裡大多數人都騎單車上班。"},{"w":"manifest","p":"v.","d":"to show something clearly","c":"顯現;表現","s":"Climate change can manifest itself in many ways, such as stronger storms, longer droughts and earlier springs.","t":"氣候變遷可能以許多方式顯現出來,例如更強的暴風雨、更長的乾旱和更早的春天。"},{"w":"prevail","p":"v.","d":"to be common or most powerful at a certain time","c":"盛行;占上風","s":"Strong winds prevail along the west coast in winter, so it is a good place to build wind farms.","t":"冬季西海岸盛行強風,所以那裡是興建風場的好地點。"},{"w":"pervasive","p":"adj.","d":"spreading widely through every part","c":"無所不在的;普遍的","s":"Plastic pollution is pervasive in the ocean, and scientists have found tiny pieces even in deep sea fish.","t":"塑膠污染在海洋中無所不在,科學家甚至在深海魚體內也發現了微小碎片。"},{"w":"ubiquitous","p":"adj.","d":"seeming to be everywhere","c":"隨處可見的","s":"Air-conditioners are ubiquitous in Taipei apartments, but they push hot air into the streets and make the city warmer.","t":"冷氣在台北的公寓裡隨處可見,但它們把熱空氣排到街上,讓城市變得更熱。"},{"w":"conventional","p":"adj.","d":"normal and traditional","c":"傳統的;常規的","s":"conventional farming uses a lot of chemicals, but some farmers are trying natural methods to protect the soil.","t":"傳統的農業使用大量化學物質,但一些農夫正嘗試自然的方法來保護土壤。"},{"w":"orthodox","p":"adj.","d":"generally accepted as correct","c":"正統的;傳統的","s":"The young engineer questioned the orthodox way of building dams, and her new design used much less concrete.","t":"這位年輕工程師質疑建造水壩的傳統方式,她的新設計使用了少得多的混凝土。"},{"w":"novel","p":"adj.","d":"new and different","c":"新穎的","s":"The students came up with a novel idea for cooling classrooms, and they won first prize at the science fair.","t":"學生們想出一個為教室降溫的新穎點子,並在科展中獲得第一名。"},{"w":"outdated","p":"adj.","d":"old and no longer useful","c":"過時的","s":"The city's flood maps are outdated, so many new homes have been built in areas that are actually dangerous.","t":"這座城市的淹水地圖已經過時,所以許多新房子蓋在其實很危險的地區。"},{"w":"tentative","p":"adj.","d":"not certain or final","c":"暫定的;試探性的","s":"The two countries reached a tentative agreement, but they still need to discuss the details next month.","t":"兩國達成了暫定的協議,但它們下個月仍需要討論細節。"},{"w":"provisional","p":"adj.","d":"arranged for now but may change later","c":"臨時的;暫定的","s":"The provisional results show that this was the hottest year ever, and the final report will come out in spring.","t":"暫定的結果顯示今年是史上最熱的一年,最終報告將於春天發布。"},{"w":"definitive","p":"adj.","d":"final and not able to be changed","c":"明確的;決定性的","s":"There is no definitive answer to the question yet, so scientists will continue to collect data for several more years.","t":"這個問題目前還沒有明確的答案,所以科學家會再繼續收集數年的資料。"},{"w":"conclusive","p":"adj.","d":"proving something without doubt","c":"確鑿的;決定性的","s":"The evidence for human-caused warming is conclusive, and almost every climate scientist agrees with it.","t":"人為造成暖化的證據是確鑿的,幾乎每位氣候科學家都同意。"},{"w":"plausible","p":"adj.","d":"seeming reasonable or likely to be true","c":"合理的;似乎可信的","s":"Her explanation for the fish deaths was plausible, but the team still tested the water to make sure.","t":"她對魚群死亡的解釋合理,但團隊仍然檢驗了水質以確認。"},{"w":"flawed","p":"adj.","d":"having mistakes or weaknesses","c":"有缺陷的","s":"The report was flawed because it used only one year of data, so other experts did not trust its conclusions.","t":"這份報告有缺陷,因為它只用了一年的數據,所以其他專家不信任它的結論。"},{"w":"impartial","p":"adj.","d":"not supporting one side more than another","c":"公正的;不偏袒的","s":"The committee must stay impartial, so none of its members can work for oil or gas companies.","t":"委員會必須保持公正,所以其成員都不能為石油或天然氣公司工作。"}]},{"unit":13,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 6 (clarity – intermediate)","cards":[{"w":"clarity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being clear and easy to understand","c":"清楚;明確","s":"Businesses want clarity about future energy rules, because they need to plan their investments for many years.","t":"企業希望未來的能源規定能更明確,因為他們需要為多年的投資做規劃。"},{"w":"nuance","p":"n.","d":"a small but important difference in meaning","c":"細微差別","s":"The debate on nuclear power needs more nuance, because it is not simply good or bad.","t":"關於核能的辯論需要更多細微的區辨,因為它並不是單純的好或壞。"},{"w":"simplistic","p":"adj.","d":"treating a problem as simpler than it really is","c":"過度簡化的","s":"Saying that planting trees will solve everything is simplistic, because we also need to cut emissions.","t":"說種樹就能解決一切是過度簡化的想法,因為我們也需要減少排放。"},{"w":"oversimplify","p":"v.","d":"to describe something in a way that is too simple","c":"過度簡化","s":"Headlines often oversimplify scientific reports, so readers may not understand how uncertain some results are.","t":"新聞標題常常過度簡化科學報告,所以讀者可能不了解某些結果有多不確定。"},{"w":"generalise","p":"v.","d":"to say something is true for all cases","c":"概括;一概而論","s":"We should not generalise from one cold winter, because climate is about long-term patterns, not a single season.","t":"我們不應該從一個寒冷的冬天就一概而論,因為氣候講的是長期模式,而不是單一季節。"},{"w":"rationale","p":"n.","d":"the reasons for a decision","c":"基本原理;理由","s":"The mayor explained the rationale for the new parking fees, and she said the money would pay for more buses.","t":"市長解釋了新停車費的理由,她說這筆錢將用來增加公車。"},{"w":"metric","p":"n.","d":"a way of measuring something","c":"指標;衡量標準","s":"Carbon per person is a useful metric, but it does not show which countries polluted the most in the past.","t":"人均碳排放是一個有用的指標,但它無法顯示哪些國家過去污染最多。"},{"w":"benchmark","p":"n.","d":"a standard used for comparison","c":"基準;標竿","s":"The new office became a benchmark for green buildings, and other companies copied many of its ideas.","t":"這棟新辦公室成為綠建築的標竿,其他公司仿效了它的許多設計。"},{"w":"parameter","p":"n.","d":"a limit or rule that controls how something is done","c":"參數;界限","s":"The model uses several parameter such as wind speed and temperature, so its forecasts are quite accurate.","t":"這個模型使用了幾個參數,例如風速和溫度,所以它的預報相當準確。"},{"w":"paradigm","p":"n.","d":"a typical model or way of thinking","c":"範式;模式","s":"Renewable energy has changed the old paradigm of power, so homes can now produce electricity as well as use it.","t":"可再生能源改變了舊有的電力模式,所以家庭現在既能用電也能發電。"},{"w":"discrete","p":"adj.","d":"clearly separate","c":"分離的;個別的","s":"The study divided the coast into discrete sections, and each part was tested for erosion separately.","t":"這項研究把海岸劃分為個別的區段,每個部分都分別進行侵蝕檢測。"},{"w":"overwhelmingly","p":"adv.","d":"very strongly; by a very large amount","c":"壓倒性地","s":"The public overwhelmingly supported the new park, so the city cancelled its plan to build a shopping mall there.","t":"民眾壓倒性地支持新公園,所以市政府取消了在那裡蓋購物中心的計畫。"},{"w":"whereby","p":"adv.","d":"by which; through which","c":"藉此;憑此","s":"The town created a system whereby people can borrow electric bikes for free, and it has reduced traffic a lot.","t":"鎮上建立了一個制度,藉此民眾可以免費借用電動自行車,而它大幅減少了車流。"},{"w":"likewise","p":"adv.","d":"in the same way","c":"同樣地","s":"Our school turned off the lights at lunchtime, and the school next door did likewise, so both saved energy.","t":"我們學校在午餐時間關燈,隔壁學校也同樣這麼做,所以兩校都節省了能源。"},{"w":"so-called","p":"adj.","d":"used to show that a name may not be accurate","c":"所謂的","s":"The so-called green bags were made of thick plastic, so they were actually worse for the environment.","t":"那些所謂的環保袋是用厚塑膠做的,所以它們其實對環境更糟。"},{"w":"unforeseen","p":"adj.","d":"not expected or predicted","c":"未預見的;意料之外的","s":"The project faced unforeseen problems, but the engineers solved them and finished the seawall on time.","t":"這項工程遇到意料之外的問題,但工程師們解決了它們並準時完成海堤。"},{"w":"undertake","p":"v.","d":"to start doing a job or task","c":"承擔;進行","s":"The university undertook a five-year study of the river, and the results helped the city plan new flood walls.","t":"這所大學進行了一項為期五年的河川研究,其結果幫助市政府規劃新的防洪牆。"},{"w":"forthcoming","p":"adj.","d":"going to happen soon","c":"即將到來的","s":"The forthcoming climate summit will be held in Asia, so many local groups are preparing to attend.","t":"即將到來的氣候高峰會將在亞洲舉行,所以許多在地團體正準備參加。"},{"w":"finite","p":"adj.","d":"having a limit","c":"有限的","s":"Oil and coal are finite resources, so the world will have to replace them sooner or later.","t":"石油和煤是有限的資源,所以世界遲早必須取代它們。"},{"w":"constant","p":"adj.","d":"happening all the time","c":"持續不斷的","s":"The village faces constant danger from rising water, but many families do not want to leave their land.","t":"這個村莊面臨上升海水持續不斷的威脅,但許多家庭不想離開他們的土地。"},{"w":"circumstance","p":"n.","d":"a fact or condition that affects a situation","c":"情況;情勢","s":"Under normal circumstance the river is calm, but after heavy rain it can rise by three metres in a few hours.","t":"在正常情況下河水很平靜,但大雨過後它可能在幾小時內上漲三公尺。"},{"w":"contrast","p":"n.","d":"a clear difference between two things","c":"對比;差異","s":"There is a sharp contrast between the cool forest and the hot city, so many families go to the mountains on weekends.","t":"涼爽的森林和炎熱的城市之間有明顯的對比,所以許多家庭週末都會上山。"},{"w":"convention","p":"n.","d":"a formal agreement between countries","c":"公約","s":"The United Nations climate convention was signed in 1992, and countries have met every year since then.","t":"聯合國氣候公約於1992年簽署,此後各國每年都會開會。"},{"w":"ideology","p":"n.","d":"a set of political ideas or beliefs","c":"意識形態","s":"Climate policy should be based on science rather than ideology, but in some countries it has become very political.","t":"氣候政策應該以科學為基礎而非意識形態,但在某些國家它已變得非常政治化。"},{"w":"intermediate","p":"adj.","d":"between two levels or stages","c":"中間的;中級的","s":"The plan has an intermediate target for 2030, so the country can check its progress before the final goal.","t":"這項計畫訂有2030年的中期目標,讓國家能在最終目標之前檢視進度。"}]},{"unit":14,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 7 (invoke – invariably)","cards":[{"w":"invoke","p":"v.","d":"to use a law or rule to support an action","c":"援引;行使","s":"The president invoke emergency powers after the flood, so the army could help with rescue work at once.","t":"水災後總統行使緊急權力,讓軍隊能立刻協助救援工作。"},{"w":"mediate","p":"v.","d":"to help two sides reach an agreement","c":"調解;斡旋","s":"A local professor agreed to mediate between the fishermen and the energy company, and both sides finally signed a deal.","t":"一位當地教授同意在漁民和能源公司之間調解,雙方最終簽署了協議。"},{"w":"regime","p":"n.","d":"a system of rules or government","c":"體制;制度","s":"The new tax regime rewards companies that pollute less, so many factories are buying cleaner machines.","t":"新的稅收制度獎勵污染較少的公司,所以許多工廠正在購買更乾淨的機器。"},{"w":"successor","p":"n.","d":"a person or thing that comes after another","c":"繼任者;後繼者","s":"The old agreement ended in 2020, and its successor sets stronger goals for every country.","t":"舊協議在2020年結束,而它的後繼協議為每個國家訂定了更強的目標。"},{"w":"unify","p":"v.","d":"to bring people or things together","c":"統一;使團結","s":"The flood helped to unify the community, because neighbours who had never spoken started to help each other.","t":"這場水災幫助團結了社區,因為從未交談過的鄰居開始互相幫忙。"},{"w":"sphere","p":"n.","d":"an area of activity or interest","c":"領域;範圍","s":"Climate change affects every sphere of life, so it is discussed in science, business and even art classes.","t":"氣候變遷影響生活的每個領域,所以它在科學、商業,甚至藝術課中都會被討論。"},{"w":"qualitative","p":"adj.","d":"about quality rather than numbers","c":"質性的;定性的","s":"The team collected qualitative data by talking to farmers, because numbers alone could not show how they felt.","t":"團隊透過與農夫交談收集了質性資料,因為光靠數字無法呈現他們的感受。"},{"w":"thesis","p":"n.","d":"a long piece of writing for a university degree","c":"論文","s":"My cousin wrote her thesis on heat in Taipei, and the city government used some of her ideas.","t":"我表姐寫了一篇關於台北高溫的論文,市政府採用了她的一些想法。"},{"w":"equate","p":"v.","d":"to think that two things are the same","c":"把…等同於","s":"Many people equate a warm winter with good weather, but it can actually harm crops and insects.","t":"許多人把暖冬等同於好天氣,但它其實可能傷害作物和昆蟲。"},{"w":"attitude","p":"n.","d":"the way you think or feel about something","c":"態度","s":"Public attitude towards electric cars has changed, and now many young people say they will never buy a petrol car.","t":"大眾對電動車的態度已經改變,現在許多年輕人說他們永遠不會買汽油車。"},{"w":"availability","p":"n.","d":"how easy something is to get or use","c":"可取得性;供應","s":"The availability of clean water is falling in some regions, so people walk further every day to find it.","t":"某些地區乾淨水源的供應正在減少,所以人們每天要走更遠才能取得。"},{"w":"comprehend","p":"v.","d":"to understand something fully","c":"理解","s":"It is hard to comprehend how fast the ice is melting, so the scientist showed us photos taken ten years apart.","t":"很難理解冰融化的速度有多快,所以這位科學家給我們看了相隔十年拍攝的照片。"},{"w":"deem","p":"v.","d":"to consider or judge something in a certain way","c":"認為;視為","s":"The bridge was deem unsafe after the earthquake, so cars had to use a road ten kilometres away.","t":"地震後這座橋被認為不安全,所以汽車必須改走十公里外的道路。"},{"w":"discern","p":"v.","d":"to notice or understand something that is not obvious","c":"察覺;辨別","s":"It is difficult to discern a clear trend from one year of data, so researchers look at records over many decades.","t":"很難從一年的數據中察覺出明確的趨勢,所以研究人員會檢視數十年的紀錄。"},{"w":"accomplish","p":"v.","d":"to succeed in doing something","c":"完成;達成","s":"The village accomplish its goal of using only solar power, and other towns are now asking how they did it.","t":"這個村莊達成了只使用太陽能的目標,其他城鎮現在都在詢問他們是怎麼做到的。"},{"w":"abate","p":"v.","d":"to become less strong","c":"減弱;緩和","s":"The rescue boats waited until the storm began to abate, and then they went out to find the missing fishermen.","t":"救援船等到暴風雨開始減弱,接著才出海搜尋失蹤的漁民。"},{"w":"hasten","p":"v.","d":"to make something happen sooner","c":"加速;促進","s":"The heat hasten the melting of the glacier, so the river flooded villages downstream in July.","t":"高溫加速了冰河的融化,所以河水在七月淹沒了下游的村莊。"},{"w":"augment","p":"v.","d":"to increase the size or value of something","c":"增加;擴大","s":"The city will augment its water supply with rainwater tanks, because the reservoir alone is no longer enough.","t":"市政府將以雨水儲水槽來擴大供水量,因為光靠水庫已經不夠了。"},{"w":"erratic","p":"adj.","d":"changing often in a way that cannot be predicted","c":"不穩定的;無規律的","s":"The weather has become very erratic in recent years, so farmers are not sure when to plant their seeds.","t":"近年來天氣變得非常不穩定,所以農夫不確定何時該播種。"},{"w":"volatile","p":"adj.","d":"likely to change suddenly","c":"多變的;不穩定的","s":"Oil prices are very volatile, so countries that use more renewable energy are better protected from sudden changes.","t":"油價非常多變,所以使用較多可再生能源的國家較不受突然變化的影響。"},{"w":"intermittent","p":"adj.","d":"stopping and starting again","c":"間歇性的","s":"Wind and solar power are intermittent, so we need batteries to store energy for times without sun or wind.","t":"風力和太陽能是間歇性的,所以我們需要電池在沒有陽光或風的時候儲存能源。"},{"w":"sporadic","p":"adj.","d":"happening only sometimes","c":"零星的;偶發的","s":"There was only sporadic rain during the spring, so the reservoirs were nearly empty by June.","t":"春天只下了零星的雨,所以到六月時水庫幾乎見底。"},{"w":"prolonged","p":"adj.","d":"lasting for a long time","c":"長期的;持久的","s":"A prolonged drought dried up the rivers, and many farmers had to sell their animals.","t":"一場長期乾旱讓河川乾涸,許多農夫不得不賣掉他們的牲畜。"},{"w":"recurrent","p":"adj.","d":"happening again and again","c":"反覆發生的","s":"recurrent flooding has damaged the old market many times, so the shop owners finally agreed to move.","t":"反覆發生的淹水多次損壞了老市場,所以店家們最終同意搬遷。"},{"w":"invariably","p":"adv.","d":"always; every time","c":"總是;一律","s":"Heavy rain invariably causes traffic jams in the city, so many people now work from home on stormy days.","t":"大雨總是造成市區交通堵塞,所以許多人現在在暴風雨的日子都在家工作。"}]},{"unit":15,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 8 (arguably – corroborate)","cards":[{"w":"arguably","p":"adv.","d":"used to say something may be true, though some may disagree","c":"可以說;按理說","s":"Climate change is arguably the biggest challenge of our time, but many people still do not think about it every day.","t":"氣候變遷可以說是我們這個時代最大的挑戰,但許多人仍然不會每天想到它。"},{"w":"conversely","p":"adv.","d":"in the opposite way","c":"相反地","s":"Some regions will get more rain; conversely, others will become much drier, so farming must change in both places.","t":"有些地區會有更多降雨;相反地,其他地區會變得更加乾燥,所以兩地的農業都必須改變。"},{"w":"thereafter","p":"adv.","d":"after that time","c":"此後;之後","s":"The factory closed in 2015, and thereafter the river slowly became clean enough for fish to return.","t":"工廠在2015年關閉,此後河川慢慢變得乾淨到足以讓魚群回來。"},{"w":"markedly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is clear and easy to notice","c":"明顯地","s":"Air quality improved markedly during the holiday, because fewer cars were on the road and factories were closed.","t":"假期期間空氣品質明顯改善,因為路上的車少了,工廠也關閉了。"},{"w":"steadily","p":"adv.","d":"gradually and in a regular way","c":"穩定地;逐步地","s":"The number of electric buses has grown steadily, and the city hopes all buses will be electric by 2030.","t":"電動公車的數量穩定地成長,市政府希望在2030年前所有公車都改為電動。"},{"w":"concurrently","p":"adv.","d":"at the same time","c":"同時地","s":"The city is building a new seawall and concurrently planting mangroves, so the coast will have two kinds of protection.","t":"市政府正在興建新海堤,並同時種植紅樹林,讓海岸擁有兩種保護。"},{"w":"respectively","p":"adv.","d":"in the same order as the things just mentioned","c":"分別地","s":"Wind and solar produced twenty and fifteen percent of the power respectively, so clean energy is growing fast.","t":"風力和太陽能分別提供了百分之二十和百分之十五的電力,所以潔淨能源成長迅速。"},{"w":"accordingly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that fits the situation","c":"相應地;因此","s":"The forecast said the storm would be strong, so the school planned accordingly and moved all classes online.","t":"預報說暴風雨會很強烈,所以學校相應地做了安排,把所有課程改為線上。"},{"w":"admittedly","p":"adv.","d":"used when you agree that something is true","c":"誠然;無可否認地","s":"admittedly, solar panels are expensive at first, but they save money on electricity for many years.","t":"誠然,太陽能板一開始很貴,但它們能在許多年間節省電費。"},{"w":"seemingly","p":"adv.","d":"appearing to be true, but perhaps not","c":"表面上;看似","s":"The river looked seemingly clean, but tests showed that it contained dangerous chemicals from the farms.","t":"這條河看似很乾淨,但檢驗顯示它含有來自農場的危險化學物質。"},{"w":"allegedly","p":"adv.","d":"said to be true, but not proved","c":"據說;據稱","s":"The company allegedly dumped waste into the sea, and the police are now checking its records.","t":"這家公司據稱把廢棄物倒入海中,警方目前正在調查它的紀錄。"},{"w":"relatively","p":"adv.","d":"compared with other things","c":"相對地;比較","s":"The changes needed are relatively simple, but they require people to give up some old habits.","t":"所需的改變相對簡單,但它們需要人們放棄一些舊習慣。"},{"w":"virtually","p":"adv.","d":"almost completely","c":"幾乎;實際上","s":"The lake had virtually disappeared by the end of summer, so the boat owners had nothing to do.","t":"到夏末時湖泊幾乎消失了,所以船主們無事可做。"},{"w":"thorough","p":"adj.","d":"careful and complete","c":"徹底的;周密的","s":"The engineers made a thorough check of the dam after the earthquake, and they found two small cracks.","t":"地震後工程師們對水壩做了徹底的檢查,並發現了兩道小裂縫。"},{"w":"meticulous","p":"adj.","d":"very careful about details","c":"一絲不苟的;細心的","s":"She kept meticulous records of the birds in her garden for thirty years, so scientists used them to study climate change.","t":"她三十年來一絲不苟地記錄自家花園裡的鳥類,所以科學家用這些紀錄來研究氣候變遷。"},{"w":"systematic","p":"adj.","d":"done according to a careful plan","c":"有系統的","s":"The team used a systematic method to count the trees, and they checked every square of the forest map.","t":"團隊使用有系統的方法計算樹木數量,並檢查了森林地圖上的每一格。"},{"w":"cohesive","p":"adj.","d":"united and working well together","c":"有凝聚力的","s":"A cohesive community recovers faster after a disaster, because neighbours share tools, food and information.","t":"有凝聚力的社區在災後復原得更快,因為鄰居們會分享工具、食物和資訊。"},{"w":"indispensable","p":"adj.","d":"too important to be without","c":"不可或缺的","s":"Weather satellites are indispensable for typhoon forecasts, so countries share their data with each other.","t":"氣象衛星對颱風預報是不可或缺的,所以各國彼此分享資料。"},{"w":"paramount","p":"adj.","d":"more important than anything else","c":"最重要的;至高無上的","s":"Safety is paramount during a typhoon, so people should stay indoors even if the wind seems weak.","t":"颱風期間安全是最重要的,所以即使風看起來很弱,人們也應該待在室內。"},{"w":"salient","p":"adj.","d":"most important or noticeable","c":"最顯著的;重要的","s":"The report listed the salient points on the first page, so busy leaders could understand it quickly.","t":"報告在第一頁列出了最重要的重點,讓忙碌的領袖們能快速理解。"},{"w":"prominent","p":"adj.","d":"important and well known","c":"著名的;重要的","s":"A prominent scientist spoke at the conference, and her warning about sea level rise made the evening news.","t":"一位著名的科學家在會議上發表演說,她對海平面上升的警告登上了晚間新聞。"},{"w":"conspicuous","p":"adj.","d":"very easy to see or notice","c":"顯眼的;明顯的","s":"The damage to the forest was conspicuous from the plane, and large brown areas stretched across the hills.","t":"從飛機上看森林的損害非常明顯,大片褐色區域橫跨整個山丘。"},{"w":"tangible","p":"adj.","d":"real and able to be seen or measured","c":"具體的;實質的","s":"Students want tangible results from the climate club, so they track how much rubbish they collect each month.","t":"學生們希望氣候社團有具體的成果,所以他們記錄每個月收集了多少垃圾。"},{"w":"refute","p":"v.","d":"to prove that something is wrong","c":"駁斥;反駁","s":"The scientist used clear data to refute the false claim, and the video was watched by millions of people.","t":"這位科學家用明確的數據駁斥了錯誤的說法,這段影片被數百萬人觀看。"},{"w":"corroborate","p":"v.","d":"to support an idea with new evidence","c":"證實;佐證","s":"Satellite images corroborate what the villagers said, because the glacier had clearly become much smaller.","t":"衛星影像證實了村民所說的話,因為冰河明顯變小了很多。"}]},{"unit":16,"theme":"Fixed Phrases & Collocations 固定片語與搭配詞","cards":[{"w":"global warming","p":"n.phr.","d":"the rise in the Earth's average temperature","c":"全球暖化","s":"global warming is making summers longer in Taiwan, so schools are thinking about starting classes earlier in the morning.","t":"全球暖化正讓台灣的夏天變得更長,所以學校正在考慮早上提早開始上課。"},{"w":"carbon footprint","p":"n.phr.","d":"the amount of carbon a person or activity produces","c":"碳足跡","s":"Flying to Europe adds a lot to your carbon footprint, so my family took a train trip around Taiwan this year.","t":"飛往歐洲會大幅增加你的碳足跡,所以我們家今年改搭火車環島旅行。"},{"w":"extreme weather","p":"n.phr.","d":"very unusual and dangerous weather","c":"極端天氣","s":"extreme weather such as floods and heatwaves is becoming more common, and cities must prepare for it.","t":"像水災和熱浪這樣的極端天氣變得越來越常見,城市必須為此做好準備。"},{"w":"tipping point","p":"n.phr.","d":"the moment when a small change causes a big, sudden effect","c":"臨界點;轉捩點","s":"Scientists fear the rainforest may reach a tipping point, and then it could slowly turn into dry grassland.","t":"科學家擔心雨林可能達到臨界點,接著它可能慢慢變成乾燥的草原。"},{"w":"a ticking time bomb","p":"n.phr.","d":"a problem that will become very serious soon","c":"定時炸彈;隨時會爆發的問題","s":"Experts call the melting permafrost a ticking time bomb, because it holds huge amounts of gas that could escape.","t":"專家把融化中的永凍土稱為一顆定時炸彈,因為它蘊含大量可能逸散的氣體。"},{"w":"for future generations","p":"phr.","d":"for people who will live after us","c":"為了後代子孫","s":"We must protect the forests for future generations, because our children and grandchildren will need clean air and water too.","t":"我們必須為了後代子孫保護森林,因為我們的孩子和孫子也會需要乾淨的空氣和水。"},{"w":"cut down on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to use or do less of something","c":"減少","s":"Our family decided to cut down on meat, because farming animals produces a lot of greenhouse gases.","t":"我們家決定減少吃肉,因為飼養動物會產生大量溫室氣體。"},{"w":"phase out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop using something gradually","c":"逐步淘汰","s":"The government plans to phase out petrol scooters by 2035, so new buyers are already choosing electric ones.","t":"政府計畫在2035年前逐步淘汰汽油機車,所以新買家已經在選擇電動機車了。"},{"w":"go green","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start living or working in a way that is better for the environment","c":"走向環保;綠化","s":"The café decided to go green last year, so it stopped using plastic straws and started selling local food.","t":"這家咖啡廳去年決定走向環保,所以它停止使用塑膠吸管並開始販售在地食材。"},{"w":"run out of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have no more of something left","c":"用完;耗盡","s":"If the rain does not come soon, the town will run out of drinking water, so people are saving every drop.","t":"如果雨再不來,鎮上就會用完飲用水,所以人們正在節約每一滴水。"},{"w":"the tip of the iceberg","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small, visible part of a much bigger problem","c":"冰山一角","s":"The flooded streets were only the tip of the iceberg, because the storm had also damaged farms and power lines.","t":"淹水的街道只是冰山一角,因為暴風雨也損壞了農場和電線。"},{"w":"weather the storm","p":"v.phr.","d":"to get through a difficult time successfully","c":"度過難關","s":"The small farm lost half its crops, but the family managed to weather the storm with help from the community.","t":"這座小農場損失了一半的作物,但這家人在社區的幫助下設法度過難關。"},{"w":"bear the brunt of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to suffer the worst part of something","c":"首當其衝;承受最大衝擊","s":"Poor coastal villages bear the brunt of rising seas, but they produced almost none of the pollution.","t":"貧窮的沿海村莊首當其衝承受海平面上升的衝擊,但它們幾乎沒有製造任何污染。"},{"w":"a race against time","p":"n.phr.","d":"a situation where you must work very fast to finish before it is too late","c":"與時間賽跑","s":"Saving the coral reef is a race against time, because the water is getting warmer every summer.","t":"拯救珊瑚礁是一場與時間賽跑,因為海水每年夏天都在變暖。"},{"w":"sound the alarm","p":"v.phr.","d":"to warn people about a danger","c":"敲響警鐘;發出警告","s":"Scientists sound the alarm about melting ice many years ago, but governments were slow to listen.","t":"科學家多年前就對融冰敲響了警鐘,但政府遲遲不願傾聽。"},{"w":"take steps to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do things in order to achieve something","c":"採取措施","s":"Our school has take steps to save energy, and we now turn off all fans when we leave the classroom.","t":"我們學校已經採取措施節約能源,現在我們離開教室時都會關掉所有電扇。"},{"w":"on the rise","p":"adj.phr.","d":"increasing","c":"正在上升;日益增加","s":"Heat-related illnesses are on the rise, so doctors advise people to drink water and stay out of the midday sun.","t":"與高溫相關的疾病正在增加,所以醫生建議民眾多喝水並避開正午的陽光。"},{"w":"in the face of","p":"phr.","d":"when dealing with a difficult situation","c":"面對","s":"in the face of rising seas, the islanders have kept their culture alive, but many young people have moved away.","t":"面對上升的海平面,島民們讓自己的文化延續下去,但許多年輕人已經搬走了。"},{"w":"lead by example","p":"v.phr.","d":"to show others how to behave by doing it yourself","c":"以身作則","s":"Our principal wanted to lead by example, so she started riding a bicycle to school every day.","t":"我們校長想要以身作則,所以她開始每天騎腳踏車上學。"},{"w":"at the expense of","p":"phr.","d":"causing harm or loss to something else","c":"以…為代價","s":"The factory grew quickly at the expense of the river, and now the water is too dirty for fish.","t":"這家工廠的快速成長是以河川為代價,現在河水髒到魚都無法生存。"}]}];
